1
00:00:05,131 --> 00:00:07,299
Morning of the X-date.

2
00:00:07,383 --> 00:00:09,009
Still before leaving.

3
00:00:09,093 --> 00:00:09,927
It's so warm.

4
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,637
The sun is intense.

5
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:14,432
Makes you really crave one of those.

6
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:15,641
A cold beer, huh?

7
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:17,935
You read my mind.

8
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,019
What else could it be?

9
00:00:19,103 --> 00:00:20,229
Thought you'd say

10
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:21,856
"chicks in bikinis" or something.

11
00:00:22,064 --> 00:00:23,566
Want that too.

12
00:00:23,649 --> 00:00:25,317
A girl in a swimsuit is coming anyway.

13
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,904
She's here. So cute.

14
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:30,448
Cute.

15
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:31,949
Looks like a school swimsuit.

16
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:35,244
Does it have her name tag on it?

17
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:37,580
So cute.

18
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:38,706
Let's all go swimming.

19
00:00:38,789 --> 00:00:40,791
Very Korean style.

20
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:43,753
Let me take a photo of you, Kanako.

21
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:46,630
Nice.

22
00:00:46,714 --> 00:00:47,548
I don't look good.

23
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,341
No, you're looking great.

24
00:00:50,426 --> 00:00:52,303
What happened yesterday?

25
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,722
I walked back thinking,

26
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:56,599
"Is there huge drama going down?"

27
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:58,058
She was curious.

28
00:00:58,142 --> 00:00:59,685
There wasn't any drama.

29
00:00:59,769 --> 00:01:00,895
That's the part.

30
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:03,606
You're dying to know, right, Kanako?

31
00:01:03,689 --> 00:01:05,191
I don't even wanna go on the date.

32
00:01:05,274 --> 00:01:06,567
Kanako-chan.

33
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:07,860
Kanako.

34
00:01:08,319 --> 00:01:09,612
What do you mean?

35
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:12,823
I mean, who wouldn't hate it?

36
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:15,242
I mean, he talks like he's 100% all-in…

37
00:01:15,326 --> 00:01:18,120
and acting like, "Once we meet again,
all I gotta do is try."

38
00:01:18,204 --> 00:01:20,498
"I'll try hard and ask you on a date."

39
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:21,832
So I waited a week and…

40
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:23,209
Why did he even call me?

41
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:24,919
Oh, so that was the setup.

42
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:27,379
Like, "Why did you call me here?
Why did I even come?"

43
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:29,048
That's what he said, huh.

44
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:30,466
I mean, I've been waiting.

45
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:32,593
To see how hard he can try.

46
00:01:32,968 --> 00:01:33,886
What a toxic guy!

47
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:35,179
Just throw him in the pool.

48
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:36,764
Go for it.

49
00:01:41,185 --> 00:01:42,102
Ouch.

50
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:43,604
Get in the pool.

51
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:45,356
Wait. Ow, ow!

52
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:47,316
Wait, ow, ow, ow!

53
00:01:47,566 --> 00:01:48,734
No jumping in the pool!

54
00:01:48,818 --> 00:01:49,819
I'm throwing him in.

55
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:53,948
He'll be totally fine getting wet.

56
00:01:54,031 --> 00:01:55,324
No, no, no!

57
00:01:55,783 --> 00:01:57,368
You absolutely can't push him in.

58
00:01:57,618 --> 00:01:58,911
'Cause it's dangerous.

59
00:01:59,245 --> 00:02:01,872
Thank you for stopping them.

60
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:04,083
I got scolded.

61
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:06,043
So no pool-pushing.

62
00:02:06,544 --> 00:02:07,878
Aw, bummer.

63
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,716
You still like him, right?

64
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,094
I thought about it a lot last night,

65
00:02:15,177 --> 00:02:16,637
but it's not like "love".

66
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:18,556
It's not?

67
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:20,724
I just don't get why
I'm getting so jealous.

68
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:21,934
That means you like him.

69
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:23,978
You've got feelings for sure.

70
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:25,563
No, it's different!

71
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:28,023
It's not different.
You're getting jealous.

72
00:02:29,191 --> 00:02:30,776
But today, I'm not sure.

73
00:02:31,402 --> 00:02:32,945
I'm dreading this date.

74
00:02:37,241 --> 00:02:39,577
I saw something awful yesterday,

75
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:41,787
so it totally killed the vibe.

76
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:46,584
I feel frustrated, lonely,

77
00:02:47,543 --> 00:02:50,170
and secretly want him to say he likes me.

78
00:02:50,254 --> 00:02:53,799
So I just get annoyed.

79
00:02:53,883 --> 00:02:55,009
That makes sense.

80
00:02:55,593 --> 00:02:56,844
Our first drive together.

81
00:02:56,927 --> 00:02:58,387
Oh, right.

82
00:02:59,263 --> 00:03:00,639
I'm nervous.

83
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:03,475
Oh, right. It was an X-date.

84
00:03:03,559 --> 00:03:04,643
Exactly.

85
00:03:11,609 --> 00:03:14,445
Their energy levels are
both a bit low, though.

86
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:17,531
So cute.

87
00:03:18,282 --> 00:03:19,658
Ah, nice!

88
00:03:19,742 --> 00:03:20,576
A wedding?

89
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:22,995
They're choosing outfit options
for the wedding.

90
00:03:23,078 --> 00:03:24,955
Nice.

91
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:26,290
Say cheese.

92
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,959
Congratulations.

93
00:03:29,043 --> 00:03:30,586
Congratulations.

94
00:03:36,592 --> 00:03:38,344
You look like a tyrant lord.

95
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,346
Just getting fat all by himself.

96
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:42,932
Well, well.

97
00:03:43,182 --> 00:03:45,351
I really wanted to go on an aquarium date.

98
00:03:45,434 --> 00:03:46,435
Oh, really?

99
00:03:46,518 --> 00:03:48,145
We had an aquarium date back then.

100
00:03:48,437 --> 00:03:49,647
We did. Yeah.

101
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,106
We went together.

102
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,775
I remember that.

103
00:03:54,276 --> 00:03:58,197
Hearing he requested an aquarium date

104
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,324
surprised me.

105
00:04:01,617 --> 00:04:05,579
It brought back memories of
before we started dating.

106
00:04:06,664 --> 00:04:11,126
When Ryochin said
at the very end of the hocance…

107
00:04:11,377 --> 00:04:15,381
"I realized I was wrong,"

108
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:18,175
I thought he'd finally become

109
00:04:19,176 --> 00:04:21,261
a real human being.

110
00:04:21,512 --> 00:04:26,433
It depends on how he acts,

111
00:04:26,892 --> 00:04:32,898
but I personally want to face
Ryo-chin properly now.

112
00:04:32,982 --> 00:04:34,024
Yes.

113
00:04:36,068 --> 00:04:39,488
My ex starts at a disadvantage
with me, right?

114
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:41,115
Right.

115
00:04:41,198 --> 00:04:46,203
Since I couldn't make her happy back then,

116
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:49,623
this trip feels like

117
00:04:49,707 --> 00:04:52,042
a journey to face

118
00:04:52,126 --> 00:04:56,171
my past mistakes.

119
00:04:57,172 --> 00:05:00,259
Misato found a fish
that looked like herself…

120
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,555
I feel connected to it.

121
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:09,226
We laugh over stupid things,

122
00:05:09,351 --> 00:05:13,981
and there's a real sense of comfort.

123
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:19,236
But honestly, there's someone else
I'm interested in too.

124
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,237
Okay.

125
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,198
At first I was all about Mao-chan, but…

126
00:05:23,282 --> 00:05:26,952
since I came here for my final love,

127
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,913
I want to explore different sides.

128
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:32,833
I'm still figuring things out.

129
00:05:34,293 --> 00:05:36,837
I really want to take

130
00:05:37,755 --> 00:05:40,591
both of them seriously.

131
00:05:41,341 --> 00:05:42,426
I see.

132
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:43,719
Takes me back.

133
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:45,179
Look, a Shisa statue.

134
00:05:45,262 --> 00:05:46,096
Yeah, a Shisa.

135
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:47,139
So cute.

136
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:49,099
This is American Village, isn't it?

137
00:05:49,183 --> 00:05:50,934
It says "Brings good family fortune."

138
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:53,604
"Build love, create a harmonious home…"

139
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:55,606
Maybe you should wear this,

140
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:56,690
not me.

141
00:05:56,774 --> 00:05:57,691
Totally.

142
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,570
Smell this.

143
00:06:05,074 --> 00:06:08,452
On family trips,
we'd always make a stop in Chatan.

144
00:06:09,203 --> 00:06:11,080
The last time Hikaru and I

145
00:06:11,163 --> 00:06:16,418
came here together was probably
16 or 17 years ago.

146
00:06:17,628 --> 00:06:19,922
Back then, everything was pure.

147
00:06:20,005 --> 00:06:23,133
No drama, no issues.

148
00:06:23,217 --> 00:06:25,677
Remembering that time

149
00:06:25,761 --> 00:06:30,182
made me feel like I was 20 years old

150
00:06:30,265 --> 00:06:32,643
all over again.

151
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:36,021
Whoa, crazy.

152
00:06:37,523 --> 00:06:39,149
Brings back memories.

153
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:42,903
I was crouching down right here,

154
00:06:42,986 --> 00:06:46,073
and you took the photo like this.

155
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:47,366
She remembers so much.

156
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:48,826
Totally.

157
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:51,578
So nostalgic!

158
00:06:51,662 --> 00:06:53,122
The exact same angle.

159
00:06:54,957 --> 00:06:56,500
You were wearing that Rodeo Crown hat!

160
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:57,918
No, it was a linen one.

161
00:06:58,001 --> 00:06:59,628
Oh, a straw hat?

162
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,505
I'm huge.

163
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:04,174
Can 17 years really change
someone this much?

164
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:09,054
It's better when he gets teased
a little like that.

165
00:07:14,518 --> 00:07:16,145
Alright, let's go!

166
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:18,313
Yay!

167
00:07:18,564 --> 00:07:20,440
Best day off ever.

168
00:07:20,524 --> 00:07:21,692
Yeah.

169
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:22,985
Thank you so much.

170
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:24,319
The absolute best.

171
00:07:24,403 --> 00:07:25,612
What should we do?

172
00:07:25,696 --> 00:07:27,865
Aren't you planning something for us?

173
00:07:28,157 --> 00:07:29,867
-Don't you have something planned?
-Me?

174
00:07:29,992 --> 00:07:31,326
Should I think of something?

175
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:32,703
No, no, no.

176
00:07:33,287 --> 00:07:35,038
We're just gonna swim.

177
00:07:35,122 --> 00:07:37,416
Oh, really? Oh.

178
00:07:37,499 --> 00:07:41,503
I got my hopes up thinking
you were gonna do something for me.

179
00:07:41,587 --> 00:07:44,548
Hold on a sec…

180
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:51,013
"Hang in there."

181
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:52,472
That's all I can say.

182
00:07:53,182 --> 00:07:56,768
"Don't give up."
That's really the only advice.

183
00:07:56,935 --> 00:07:58,979
But if I get crushed by
something like this,

184
00:07:59,062 --> 00:08:02,149
I'll never make it
long-term with Yoko-chan.

185
00:08:03,442 --> 00:08:05,360
I'm so excited!

186
00:08:05,444 --> 00:08:07,779
Don't set the bar too high.

187
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:09,448
I love how they are.

188
00:08:09,573 --> 00:08:10,699
Awkward every time.

189
00:08:10,782 --> 00:08:13,285
That awkwardness is what makes it so good.

190
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:17,706
Wow.

191
00:08:17,956 --> 00:08:20,500
We landed!

192
00:08:20,584 --> 00:08:21,585
This is amazing!

193
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:22,544
This is so nice!

194
00:08:22,628 --> 00:08:23,795
Absolutely gorgeous.

195
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,923
So beautiful.

196
00:08:26,006 --> 00:08:28,133
It's so beautiful it's making me laugh.

197
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:29,343
Beautiful.

198
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:32,721
Look how crystal clear
the water is right here.

199
00:08:33,722 --> 00:08:35,724
What a beautiful sandy beach.

200
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:52,032
Feels so amazing.

201
00:08:53,283 --> 00:08:54,576
Incredible.

202
00:08:59,748 --> 00:09:01,416
Hey.

203
00:09:01,917 --> 00:09:04,169
It was incredibly beautiful.

204
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:06,046
So, Yoko-chan…

205
00:09:07,965 --> 00:09:09,466
Tada!

206
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:11,551
Go ahead and open it.

207
00:09:11,635 --> 00:09:12,803
What is it?

208
00:09:13,011 --> 00:09:15,055
Isn't it "T"?

209
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,098
It's "T".

210
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:17,557
No way!

211
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,477
"Happy Birthday."

212
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,689
"I treasure the wonderful Yoko
more than anyone."

213
00:09:23,772 --> 00:09:25,065
That's what I wrote.

214
00:09:25,774 --> 00:09:26,608
This is so nice.

215
00:09:27,943 --> 00:09:29,486
You prepared this for me?

216
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:31,280
Yeah. All the way from Yokohama.

217
00:09:31,363 --> 00:09:32,531
Really?

218
00:09:32,614 --> 00:09:34,866
I've been carrying it with me
the whole time.

219
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:40,289
We used to celebrate her birthday
every year as friends,

220
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:44,668
but I couldn't celebrate her birthday
last year.

221
00:09:44,751 --> 00:09:48,297
So I was thinking I really wanted to

222
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,799
give her a present.

223
00:09:51,049 --> 00:09:53,468
I don't know what will happen with us,

224
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:56,388
but I hope whenever she sees this,

225
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:59,266
she remembers the time

226
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:02,644
we spent together on this hocance.

227
00:10:02,728 --> 00:10:05,272
It'd be even better

228
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:08,775
if we could go home together
and laugh about

229
00:10:08,859 --> 00:10:10,277
all of this later.

230
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,862
So that wasn't an awkward smirk.

231
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,405
It was a smug grin!

232
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:16,616
I see. Since she said she expected him
to do something.

233
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,869
"I've got something planned."

234
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:21,705
It's a vase.

235
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:23,332
So cute!

236
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:25,917
Pretty cute, right?

237
00:10:26,001 --> 00:10:27,461
Super cute.

238
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:28,628
And…

239
00:10:28,712 --> 00:10:29,629
Wow.

240
00:10:30,005 --> 00:10:31,006
A single rose.

241
00:10:31,715 --> 00:10:33,050
For you.

242
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:34,134
Wow.

243
00:10:34,217 --> 00:10:36,845
Did you know Tiffany blue
comes from the robin?

244
00:10:37,346 --> 00:10:40,140
Apparently, robins are birds
that bring happiness.

245
00:10:41,058 --> 00:10:42,559
So I figured…

246
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,560
I see.

247
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,687
This vase could

248
00:10:45,771 --> 00:10:47,105
remind me to

249
00:10:47,189 --> 00:10:49,441
be a bigger man…

250
00:10:49,524 --> 00:10:52,819
a man with the capacity
to hold everything.

251
00:10:53,362 --> 00:10:56,156
And I really want to see you bloom
in so many different ways,

252
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:58,075
Yoko.

253
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:01,453
I felt like this represents us,

254
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:06,666
me being the vase
that brings you happiness…

255
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:09,961
Wow, there's so much meaning behind this.

256
00:11:10,045 --> 00:11:12,089
…so I bought it with that in mind.

257
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:14,800
I'm surprised.

258
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:15,717
It was worth it

259
00:11:16,259 --> 00:11:17,469
if it made you happy.

260
00:11:17,552 --> 00:11:18,428
What a surprise.

261
00:11:18,512 --> 00:11:19,388
Yeah.

262
00:11:19,471 --> 00:11:21,139
So…

263
00:11:21,223 --> 00:11:24,267
Even if it's…

264
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:28,980
hard for your feelings for me

265
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:32,526
to spark right now…

266
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,862
I still only have eyes for you.

267
00:11:36,071 --> 00:11:38,698
I want us to go home together

268
00:11:41,118 --> 00:11:43,286
and continue our relationship.

269
00:11:48,917 --> 00:11:50,544
That really hit home for her.

270
00:11:51,545 --> 00:11:53,088
I think it went great.

271
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,756
I think she was truly happy.

272
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:57,467
I thought the vase was beautiful,

273
00:11:57,551 --> 00:11:59,261
and she really loved it too.

274
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:02,431
The idea of a flower vase

275
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:04,474
just clicked for me.

276
00:12:04,558 --> 00:12:07,894
It was like a stroke of inspiration.

277
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:13,275
The way she looks at me

278
00:12:13,358 --> 00:12:16,111
has definitely changed today.

279
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:19,156
My heart is full,
and I'm totally satisfied.

280
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:22,909
Today was such a wonderful time.

281
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:26,288
It's so pretty. Thank you so much.

282
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:27,330
Don't mention it.

283
00:12:27,414 --> 00:12:29,291
I didn't know you had a poetic side.

284
00:12:30,459 --> 00:12:31,293
Wow.

285
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:32,669
I do happen to have one, yes.

286
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:34,254
You do, huh.

287
00:12:35,922 --> 00:12:37,632
Please don't get ahead of yourself.

288
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:39,050
Right.

289
00:12:39,134 --> 00:12:41,011
Guys get cocky way too fast.

290
00:12:41,303 --> 00:12:42,554
Depends on the guy.

291
00:12:43,513 --> 00:12:44,723
Like, "Heck yeah!"

292
00:12:45,474 --> 00:12:48,226
"I nailed it! I sealed the deal today!"

293
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:50,395
Like, "Goal!"

294
00:12:53,315 --> 00:12:56,693
Earlier, you said

295
00:12:57,027 --> 00:13:00,822
you were nervous to talk to me.

296
00:13:00,906 --> 00:13:02,949
What makes you nervous?

297
00:13:04,868 --> 00:13:06,411
Oh, about what?

298
00:13:07,454 --> 00:13:10,290
Go for it, Kana-chan. Just lay it all out.

299
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:12,501
Nervous… well…

300
00:13:13,335 --> 00:13:15,462
I was wondering
what makes you feel that way.

301
00:13:18,757 --> 00:13:22,260
To be honest, part of it is
just hard to put into words.

302
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:23,887
Everything is hard.

303
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,388
It is.

304
00:13:25,514 --> 00:13:28,016
Put in the effort and spell it out.

305
00:13:28,767 --> 00:13:30,185
Well…

306
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:33,522
Getting to know
the good sides of other girls

307
00:13:34,773 --> 00:13:39,861
made my feelings sway.

308
00:13:40,403 --> 00:13:46,451
Because I got caught up in that,

309
00:13:46,785 --> 00:13:50,872
I guess I stopped making time

310
00:13:51,957 --> 00:13:55,001
for just the two of us.

311
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,379
I think that's the reason.

312
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:04,052
Is that it?

313
00:14:04,135 --> 00:14:05,262
For now, yeah.

314
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:07,514
That's the same thing as last time.

315
00:14:07,597 --> 00:14:09,307
Yeah.

316
00:14:11,726 --> 00:14:13,645
From the very start,

317
00:14:13,937 --> 00:14:18,650
I never felt like
you were 100% all-in on me.

318
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:21,152
Well, that's not true.

319
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:22,195
Bullshit.

320
00:14:22,279 --> 00:14:23,947
I'm being honest.

321
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:29,995
You didn't even try to
get to know me first.

322
00:14:30,495 --> 00:14:33,665
Honestly, you don't even know who I am.

323
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:38,920
I wanted you to get to know me first

324
00:14:40,672 --> 00:14:42,424
before exploring other options.

325
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:46,886
I'm really sorry.

326
00:14:46,970 --> 00:14:50,223
Honestly, looking back,

327
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:54,185
I really did have a blast
every single day.

328
00:14:55,687 --> 00:14:57,105
But…

329
00:14:57,480 --> 00:15:02,110
the person I wanted to talk to the most
was always you, Satoshi.

330
00:15:02,277 --> 00:15:04,112
That's so sad.

331
00:15:06,573 --> 00:15:10,619
I came here hoping
maybe we'd end up flying back to

332
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:15,290
Fukuoka together.

333
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:18,501
I got way too complacent.

334
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:21,671
I just assumed you'd come to me.

335
00:15:22,172 --> 00:15:23,757
I got my hopes up.

336
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:28,345
To be real,

337
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:32,390
I saw all your good sides

338
00:15:32,641 --> 00:15:35,435
and genuinely fell for you,

339
00:15:36,895 --> 00:15:40,357
but by that time, Satoshi, you were

340
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,858
already into someone else.

341
00:15:42,025 --> 00:15:45,570
I just want to be number one.

342
00:15:46,071 --> 00:15:49,199
I want a guy who puts me first,

343
00:15:49,282 --> 00:15:51,660
who makes me his top priority,

344
00:15:51,743 --> 00:15:53,578
and prioritizes me above everything else.

345
00:15:53,662 --> 00:15:56,081
I don't care if you talk to other girls,

346
00:15:56,164 --> 00:15:57,874
as long as I'm your top choice.

347
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:01,169
But I wasn't your top choice at all.

348
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,005
The guy I thought was focused on me

349
00:16:04,089 --> 00:16:06,091
turned around and went for someone else.

350
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:10,679
But…

351
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:13,890
coming on this hocance

352
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,393
really made me see my own flaws,

353
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:18,228
exactly the ones you saw in me.

354
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:22,440
It's so embarrassing and frustrating,

355
00:16:22,524 --> 00:16:25,151
but I'm glad I realized it.

356
00:16:25,235 --> 00:16:27,612
I really need to work on myself.

357
00:16:29,781 --> 00:16:32,325
Plus,

358
00:16:34,244 --> 00:16:37,580
I almost never catch feelings for anyone.

359
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:42,877
I haven't dated for over three years,

360
00:16:43,712 --> 00:16:46,005
but coming here,

361
00:16:46,089 --> 00:16:49,926
I was actually able to like someone again.

362
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:51,636
There were days where I really had

363
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:52,971
feelings for you.

364
00:16:53,096 --> 00:16:56,641
And for me, that was huge growth.

365
00:16:57,308 --> 00:16:59,561
So I'm really glad about that.

366
00:17:03,982 --> 00:17:05,108
You okay?

367
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:06,317
Yeah, I'm good.

368
00:17:07,485 --> 00:17:09,446
You have so many great qualities.

369
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:13,700
I just don't get why

370
00:17:13,992 --> 00:17:15,452
you get so timid

371
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:17,912
and hesitant at moments like this.

372
00:17:19,414 --> 00:17:20,373
You're great…

373
00:17:20,457 --> 00:17:21,791
Most guys don't hesitate?

374
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:25,795
Probably not to this extent.

375
00:17:25,879 --> 00:17:28,214
Wouldn't you be the same
if the roles were reversed?

376
00:17:30,175 --> 00:17:34,888
Being real with someone is so important.

377
00:17:35,305 --> 00:17:39,142
Especially if you date other women
down the line.

378
00:17:39,309 --> 00:17:42,270
So while you have the chance,
shouldn't you work on that

379
00:17:46,316 --> 00:17:49,194
and fix it before going back to Fukuoka?

380
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:55,909
I knew I'd regret it
if I didn't speak my mind.

381
00:17:57,202 --> 00:17:59,913
I've never felt this way before,

382
00:18:00,205 --> 00:18:01,831
so it was painful.

383
00:18:02,165 --> 00:18:03,875
Really painful.

384
00:18:05,168 --> 00:18:08,213
But I could never bring myself
to hate you.

385
00:18:08,296 --> 00:18:12,050
I just honestly want us
to be on good terms.

386
00:18:13,802 --> 00:18:18,181
In the end, I'm glad
things played out this way.

387
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:22,227
They really had a serious
heart-to-heart there.

388
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:25,271
Kanako-san is just so thoughtful and kind.

389
00:18:25,355 --> 00:18:27,649
Satoshi just botched his opening move,
that's all.

390
00:18:28,525 --> 00:18:30,777
True, it was just bad timing on his part.

391
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:33,780
Exploring other romantic options
is totally fair game here.

392
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:37,450
Take Hiroyoshi-san…

393
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:40,328
I thought he had a childish side,

394
00:18:40,411 --> 00:18:42,038
but…

395
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:45,166
that birthday gift? That was pure class.

396
00:18:45,667 --> 00:18:49,379
Preparing that all the way from Yokohama
was such a pro move.

397
00:18:49,462 --> 00:18:51,714
Though we still don't know where Yoko

398
00:18:51,798 --> 00:18:53,591
truly stands.

399
00:18:53,675 --> 00:18:55,218
Meanwhile, Ryo and Misato

400
00:18:55,301 --> 00:18:57,220
went on that aquarium date.

401
00:18:57,470 --> 00:19:01,599
Ryo apologized properly the other day.

402
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:03,768
But Misato seems like

403
00:19:03,852 --> 00:19:06,646
the type to hold onto memorable moments.

404
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:08,106
I see.

405
00:19:08,189 --> 00:19:10,692
People like me or Sensei…

406
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:11,860
"Sensei"?

407
00:19:11,943 --> 00:19:13,194
don't

408
00:19:13,444 --> 00:19:15,196
really forget.

409
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,283
You don't forget negative experiences
from the past easily.

410
00:19:18,366 --> 00:19:21,786
Right now they're in
a bit of a honeymoon phase,

411
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:24,414
but I wonder

412
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:28,251
if old issues will resurface
once things settle down.

413
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:31,588
After all, Misato and Ryo have been
broken up for 23 years.

414
00:19:31,796 --> 00:19:35,049
You have to wonder
how much baggage is still lingering.

415
00:19:37,385 --> 00:19:39,846
Cheers.

416
00:19:43,391 --> 00:19:44,434
Tastes good.

417
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:46,311
How was the aquarium?

418
00:19:46,394 --> 00:19:49,063
It was really nice.

419
00:19:49,147 --> 00:19:51,357
You said you don't have
any good memories together,

420
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:54,110
so I thought it'd be great

421
00:19:54,903 --> 00:19:57,322
to create a fun one.

422
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:59,782
That's why I wanted to
take you to the aquarium.

423
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:02,744
I just hoped it helped you

424
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:05,204
walk down memory lane in a nice way.

425
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,206
I see.

426
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:09,292
Pretty serious, right?

427
00:20:09,375 --> 00:20:10,627
Yeah.

428
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:12,545
Surprisingly so.

429
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:14,339
Was I like that back in the day?

430
00:20:14,422 --> 00:20:16,758
Hell no, you were nothing like this.

431
00:20:16,883 --> 00:20:18,051
You were a prickly asshole.

432
00:20:18,134 --> 00:20:19,218
Me?

433
00:20:19,802 --> 00:20:21,638
Total prickly asshole.

434
00:20:22,847 --> 00:20:24,515
Back then I'd be like,

435
00:20:24,599 --> 00:20:26,476
"Why should we hold hands?"

436
00:20:26,851 --> 00:20:29,020
If someone says that to you on a date,

437
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:31,814
it totally kills the vibe.

438
00:20:31,898 --> 00:20:34,567
Literally anyone would feel hurt by that.

439
00:20:34,817 --> 00:20:37,946
But that's just who I used to be.

440
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:43,493
So this time, I wanted a fresh start…

441
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,495
to give us the fun date

442
00:20:46,079 --> 00:20:49,707
we never got to have back then.

443
00:20:49,791 --> 00:20:52,752
That's how I wanted to approach today.

444
00:20:53,336 --> 00:20:56,381
We didn't hold hands or anything today,

445
00:20:56,464 --> 00:20:59,258
but we snapped some photos together.

446
00:21:00,009 --> 00:21:02,053
And I don't think

447
00:21:02,136 --> 00:21:04,931
she looked annoyed at me even once today.

448
00:21:05,223 --> 00:21:07,767
We were laughing all day,

449
00:21:07,850 --> 00:21:11,187
so I'd say it went really well.

450
00:21:11,479 --> 00:21:13,272
He's really stepping up.

451
00:21:13,356 --> 00:21:15,650
Yeah, he's actually making an effort.

452
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:18,903
You can tell he truly wants to change.

453
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,824
I don't know, but say…

454
00:21:23,491 --> 00:21:25,868
hypothetically, we got back together
after this.

455
00:21:26,369 --> 00:21:28,079
I really want to change,

456
00:21:28,162 --> 00:21:29,539
but doing

457
00:21:29,622 --> 00:21:32,166
a complete 180 overnight is tough.

458
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:34,669
And you mentioned
I don't communicate enough.

459
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:38,423
So…

460
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,050
if we hit a bump,

461
00:21:41,134 --> 00:21:42,635
we should actually talk it out.

462
00:21:43,219 --> 00:21:45,930
Like, "What didn't you like?"

463
00:21:46,431 --> 00:21:48,307
Or something like that.

464
00:21:48,391 --> 00:21:50,727
We never used to handle things like that.

465
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:51,728
Nope, never.

466
00:21:51,853 --> 00:21:55,148
It was always like, "Why are you mad now?"

467
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:59,527
The only time you let it all out

468
00:21:59,610 --> 00:22:02,864
was when we got drinks
with our two friends.

469
00:22:03,114 --> 00:22:06,576
Yeah. Having them step in
was the only way,

470
00:22:07,035 --> 00:22:10,872
because we couldn't
talk to each other alone.

471
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:13,583
We wouldn't have even tried.

472
00:22:13,666 --> 00:22:16,169
That's why I brought them in.

473
00:22:16,836 --> 00:22:21,382
That was the first time
I voiced what hurt me,

474
00:22:21,466 --> 00:22:24,594
but honestly, I think I was
just that intimidated by you.

475
00:22:25,803 --> 00:22:30,266
Maybe I was trying to act like
an old-school…

476
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:32,143
Yeah, I think so.

477
00:22:32,226 --> 00:22:34,312
…macho guy,

478
00:22:34,395 --> 00:22:37,565
thinking that was cool.

479
00:22:38,399 --> 00:22:42,403
Expecting the girl to just
follow two steps behind.

480
00:22:42,487 --> 00:22:45,198
Pretty much. Classic old-school

481
00:22:45,281 --> 00:22:47,075
dominant boyfriend.

482
00:22:47,575 --> 00:22:50,828
Well, it's been nearly
a quarter-century since then, so…

483
00:22:50,912 --> 00:22:53,831
maybe I've at least
made it into the 2010s.

484
00:22:53,915 --> 00:22:56,000
Probably not quite up to
2020s standards, but…

485
00:22:56,084 --> 00:22:58,377
If you've made it to the 2010s,
that's something.

486
00:22:58,461 --> 00:23:00,379
There's still hope for you.

487
00:23:02,673 --> 00:23:03,841
What should we do, though?

488
00:23:03,925 --> 00:23:04,842
What do you mean?

489
00:23:04,926 --> 00:23:08,471
What if we actually date?
It'd be so damn awkward!

490
00:23:08,638 --> 00:23:11,099
Awkward? Really?

491
00:23:12,558 --> 00:23:15,728
So if you look at the odds right now,

492
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:19,524
like percentages split between all five…

493
00:23:22,110 --> 00:23:25,696
I guess you've got
the highest chance with me.

494
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:27,532
Because right now,

495
00:23:28,241 --> 00:23:30,743
I've got it narrowed down to
just you and one other girl.

496
00:23:34,914 --> 00:23:37,166
Oof, bad move!

497
00:23:38,459 --> 00:23:40,753
Of course she's gonna be like, "huh?"

498
00:23:40,837 --> 00:23:42,255
Like, "There's another option?"

499
00:23:43,381 --> 00:23:44,841
I was just like…

500
00:23:44,924 --> 00:23:46,801
"Ugh, really?"

501
00:23:46,884 --> 00:23:50,304
I don't even think he's the type
who should be playing the field like that.

502
00:23:50,638 --> 00:23:53,474
Maybe he's keeping a backup option,
I don't know.

503
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:56,394
Q: WHO DO YOU THINK THE OTHER GIRL IS?

504
00:23:56,477 --> 00:23:57,812
Mao?

505
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:01,315
She's upbeat, cheerful,

506
00:24:01,399 --> 00:24:05,903
and just blurts out
whatever's on her mind.

507
00:24:06,821 --> 00:24:09,198
I think she's quite his type.

508
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:12,660
So that's one of the reasons
he's trying to change,

509
00:24:12,910 --> 00:24:14,996
and not just for my sake.

510
00:24:15,496 --> 00:24:19,792
If I'm still in the running,

511
00:24:20,751 --> 00:24:22,962
then of course I'd want him to pick me.

512
00:24:23,045 --> 00:24:26,632
I'm just left wondering
what kind of "two options"

513
00:24:27,216 --> 00:24:29,135
is he even talking about?

514
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:33,055
Keeping two options open is
totally fair game on this hocance.

515
00:24:33,139 --> 00:24:34,515
He's not wrong for doing it.

516
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:36,267
But should he really say it out loud?

517
00:24:36,350 --> 00:24:38,436
Yeah, you shouldn't say that to her face.

518
00:24:38,519 --> 00:24:40,021
Right.

519
00:24:42,857 --> 00:24:46,027
Wow, this is pure luxury.

520
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,820
This is insane.

521
00:24:48,779 --> 00:24:50,072
Honestly…

522
00:24:50,156 --> 00:24:51,949
Hikaru and Mao.

523
00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:53,409
So nostalgic.

524
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:54,493
Wow.

525
00:24:57,205 --> 00:24:58,748
The sun is setting.

526
00:25:01,417 --> 00:25:05,504
I've spent so long
bottling up my feelings for him,

527
00:25:06,130 --> 00:25:10,384
so part of me could
easily get swept away again.

528
00:25:11,719 --> 00:25:12,887
I brought this with me.

529
00:25:14,555 --> 00:25:17,892
My true feelings are written right here.

530
00:25:18,309 --> 00:25:20,811
If we live together

531
00:25:20,895 --> 00:25:24,315
and he handles everything
right where I can see it,

532
00:25:24,398 --> 00:25:26,525
I'd feel a lot more secure.

533
00:25:26,692 --> 00:25:29,654
Then there's his tone,

534
00:25:29,737 --> 00:25:32,240
and how he can be kind of domineering…

535
00:25:32,323 --> 00:25:35,952
I've told him forever that I hate that.

536
00:25:36,661 --> 00:25:39,580
I refuse to compromise on this.

537
00:25:39,664 --> 00:25:41,832
There are issues we have to face head-on.

538
00:25:41,916 --> 00:25:45,211
If we don't,

539
00:25:45,461 --> 00:25:47,213
I just can't picture a future together.

540
00:25:47,296 --> 00:25:49,840
You really have to separate

541
00:25:49,924 --> 00:25:52,843
your emotions from the practical reality.

542
00:25:52,927 --> 00:25:56,264
I don't know what he'll say to that,

543
00:25:56,430 --> 00:25:58,975
but I'll base my final decision
on his answer.

544
00:25:59,058 --> 00:26:01,060
Totally.

545
00:26:01,143 --> 00:26:02,812
This is reality.

546
00:26:02,895 --> 00:26:06,232
Especially with the kids involved.

547
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:09,860
They need to talk about
moving overseas ASAP.

548
00:26:09,944 --> 00:26:11,487
Yes.

549
00:26:12,488 --> 00:26:13,447
First time seeing.

550
00:26:13,531 --> 00:26:16,367
We've never been to
this side of Chatan at night.

551
00:26:16,450 --> 00:26:17,743
Never.

552
00:26:25,209 --> 00:26:28,129
Throughout this hocance,

553
00:26:28,421 --> 00:26:31,507
I know you've been trying to

554
00:26:33,217 --> 00:26:36,721
treat me right.

555
00:26:37,179 --> 00:26:41,392
And regarding the money you dipped into…

556
00:26:42,018 --> 00:26:43,686
like I always say,

557
00:26:43,811 --> 00:26:47,523
you can just earn it back.

558
00:26:49,442 --> 00:26:52,111
But because it came with lies

559
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:54,280
and betrayal,

560
00:26:55,114 --> 00:26:57,616
it made me think,
"I can't do this anymore."

561
00:26:58,617 --> 00:27:02,038
But holding onto that forever

562
00:27:03,205 --> 00:27:05,291
won't change the past.

563
00:27:06,417 --> 00:27:09,086
What's done is done.

564
00:27:10,171 --> 00:27:15,384
So, assuming you
still want to make amends,

565
00:27:15,551 --> 00:27:18,346
I actually made

566
00:27:18,846 --> 00:27:21,724
a bulleted list…

567
00:27:21,807 --> 00:27:25,311
of exactly what I need from you, Hikaru.

568
00:27:27,855 --> 00:27:31,067
The very first thing I wrote is
that we live together.

569
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:35,946
We've talked about that forever,

570
00:27:36,030 --> 00:27:38,574
but we never actually put

571
00:27:38,741 --> 00:27:41,369
all our cards on the table.

572
00:27:41,535 --> 00:27:44,288
Like our incomes,
or the debt you're carrying.

573
00:27:45,289 --> 00:27:49,001
We never really knew
how much the other was making

574
00:27:49,085 --> 00:27:52,004
or contributing to the house.

575
00:27:52,713 --> 00:27:54,256
Back then,

576
00:27:54,507 --> 00:27:56,675
part of me thought if you knew,

577
00:27:56,759 --> 00:27:58,386
you'd take it all.

578
00:27:58,469 --> 00:28:00,638
I mean, to be fair, I was taking it.

579
00:28:00,721 --> 00:28:02,348
Yeah, so…

580
00:28:02,431 --> 00:28:05,267
That's why we kept things vague.

581
00:28:06,102 --> 00:28:10,231
But if we're seriously considering
a future together,

582
00:28:10,314 --> 00:28:12,650
I want us to sit down with our bank books

583
00:28:12,733 --> 00:28:15,236
like a financial meeting.

584
00:28:16,487 --> 00:28:18,406
We designate exactly what goes where.

585
00:28:18,489 --> 00:28:20,950
"This is for the kids' school."

586
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:24,453
"This pile is absolutely untouchable."

587
00:28:24,537 --> 00:28:28,916
I think we really need that
clear separation.

588
00:28:32,753 --> 00:28:34,130
Yeah.

589
00:28:35,089 --> 00:28:36,340
You're right.

590
00:28:38,551 --> 00:28:42,638
And also, the way you
phrase things sometimes,

591
00:28:43,305 --> 00:28:44,640
you know?

592
00:28:44,932 --> 00:28:47,518
Like how you talked to me

593
00:28:47,935 --> 00:28:51,355
at the farm today.

594
00:28:51,439 --> 00:28:53,691
When you talk to me like that,

595
00:28:53,774 --> 00:28:56,193
it's so much easier to
just listen and take it in.

596
00:28:57,570 --> 00:28:59,572
It makes me way more open-minded.

597
00:28:59,655 --> 00:29:03,701
I really want you to keep that up.

598
00:29:07,496 --> 00:29:13,669
I want you to really think about
everything we've talked about.

599
00:29:15,796 --> 00:29:19,967
Hearing your final answer

600
00:29:20,092 --> 00:29:23,804
will help me decide what my next step is.

601
00:29:29,894 --> 00:29:31,645
What do you think, Hikaru?

602
00:29:34,607 --> 00:29:35,941
Well…

603
00:29:37,401 --> 00:29:40,988
When I think about the rest of my life,

604
00:29:42,698 --> 00:29:44,575
I realize

605
00:29:45,576 --> 00:29:47,328
I really want you by my side.

606
00:29:49,371 --> 00:29:51,499
When we got married, you told me,

607
00:29:52,166 --> 00:29:54,460
"I will make you happy."

608
00:29:55,961 --> 00:29:57,087
Yeah.

609
00:29:57,171 --> 00:29:58,297
That's what you told me.

610
00:29:58,464 --> 00:29:59,882
But I was just like,

611
00:29:59,965 --> 00:30:03,177
"I don't know if I can make you happy,
but I'll try."

612
00:30:03,719 --> 00:30:06,472
And looking back, that dynamic played out

613
00:30:08,057 --> 00:30:09,808
exactly how you'd expect.

614
00:30:10,726 --> 00:30:15,564
At the expense of your own life,

615
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:19,401
you stood by me,

616
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:24,448
supported me,

617
00:30:24,532 --> 00:30:27,117
and kept cheering me on
until the very end.

618
00:30:28,410 --> 00:30:31,497
Now it's my turn to

619
00:30:32,665 --> 00:30:35,793
support you.

620
00:30:38,128 --> 00:30:42,216
Honestly, I don't want to be far away.

621
00:30:42,299 --> 00:30:44,301
I want to support you by your side.

622
00:30:46,762 --> 00:30:49,932
I want to make you happy

623
00:30:51,183 --> 00:30:54,979
with my own two hands.

624
00:30:55,938 --> 00:30:58,524
It goes without saying, but…

625
00:30:58,607 --> 00:31:02,236
obviously, I need to pay back

626
00:31:02,319 --> 00:31:03,946
the money I dipped into.

627
00:31:05,781 --> 00:31:09,827
We still have time left on this vacation,
but this might be our last chance

628
00:31:09,910 --> 00:31:12,246
to spend time together just the two of us,

629
00:31:12,788 --> 00:31:16,417
so I wanted to make sure
I got my true feelings across.

630
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:24,216
What?

631
00:31:25,217 --> 00:31:26,385
Wow.

632
00:31:26,468 --> 00:31:28,220
Amazing.

633
00:31:50,951 --> 00:31:52,911
Incredible.

634
00:32:02,796 --> 00:32:05,883
I know calling it a "normal family"
sounds weird, but…

635
00:32:05,966 --> 00:32:10,471
I used to talk about things most people
take for granted like they were automatic.

636
00:32:10,554 --> 00:32:13,557
I was a guy who couldn't even
manage those basic things,

637
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:15,476
like actually living together.

638
00:32:15,893 --> 00:32:19,480
If I said I didn't want to chase
my dreams abroad, I'd be lying.

639
00:32:19,563 --> 00:32:23,776
But when I look at balancing
my career and my family,

640
00:32:24,401 --> 00:32:27,237
I realize I need to face this head-on.

641
00:32:28,072 --> 00:32:29,698
Living together…

642
00:32:30,115 --> 00:32:32,076
being right by her side.

643
00:32:33,035 --> 00:32:37,331
That feels like the most important thing
I need right now.

644
00:33:03,232 --> 00:33:05,192
So many thoughts…

645
00:33:14,910 --> 00:33:20,374
Mao was so specific about what she needs

646
00:33:20,457 --> 00:33:23,961
if they're gonna make this work.

647
00:33:24,044 --> 00:33:26,046
Seriously,

648
00:33:26,130 --> 00:33:32,010
you can really feel the raw reality of
people in their mid-30s.

649
00:33:32,094 --> 00:33:33,262
Totally.

650
00:33:33,429 --> 00:33:36,515
I've never seen anyone pull out
a list like that for a first marriage.

651
00:33:37,349 --> 00:33:39,017
After everything they've been through.

652
00:33:39,101 --> 00:33:40,936
Too intense for a first marriage.

653
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,730
It shows they've been through a lot.

654
00:33:43,063 --> 00:33:46,066
It's a huge compromise.

655
00:33:46,150 --> 00:33:48,652
Mao's basically saying,

656
00:33:48,736 --> 00:33:50,529
"I'll lay everything out if you do too."

657
00:33:50,612 --> 00:33:52,865
For sure.

658
00:33:52,990 --> 00:33:57,411
"I'll try my best" or "I love you"

659
00:33:57,494 --> 00:34:00,247
isn't enough anymore at this point.

660
00:34:00,372 --> 00:34:04,001
I really want him to
thoroughly digest that list

661
00:34:04,084 --> 00:34:07,463
and process it in his head…

662
00:34:07,546 --> 00:34:09,631
Just go over it one more time.

663
00:34:09,715 --> 00:34:12,760
…and whether he can actually
hold onto that commitment

664
00:34:13,051 --> 00:34:15,012
to make things work,

665
00:34:15,095 --> 00:34:17,723
that's going to be the next major hurdle.

666
00:34:20,142 --> 00:34:21,143
Hey, we're back.

667
00:34:21,268 --> 00:34:22,561
Welcome back.

668
00:34:22,686 --> 00:34:24,104
We're back.

669
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,148
Hey. Just the two of you?

670
00:34:26,273 --> 00:34:27,566
It's been a while.

671
00:34:27,649 --> 00:34:29,818
So long.

672
00:34:30,652 --> 00:34:31,945
Everyone's not back yet?

673
00:34:32,029 --> 00:34:33,030
Not yet.

674
00:34:33,322 --> 00:34:34,490
Where did you guys go?

675
00:34:34,573 --> 00:34:35,949
What have you been up to?

676
00:34:36,033 --> 00:34:36,867
Did you eat dinner?

677
00:34:36,950 --> 00:34:37,785
Yeah.

678
00:34:37,868 --> 00:34:39,453
We're figuring out what to do next.

679
00:34:39,995 --> 00:34:41,455
You guys took a ton of photos.

680
00:34:41,747 --> 00:34:45,125
We sure did.

681
00:34:46,293 --> 00:34:49,171
Champagne and picnic. Alone.

682
00:34:49,463 --> 00:34:50,756
Doesn't his back look lonely?

683
00:34:50,839 --> 00:34:52,424
Looks like he gave it everything.

684
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:54,510
He's looking pretty relaxed now.

685
00:34:54,593 --> 00:34:55,469
Yeah.

686
00:34:56,678 --> 00:34:58,347
Why'd you take a picture of me alone?

687
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:02,142
I don't know. You were by yourself,
so I snapped it.

688
00:35:02,810 --> 00:35:04,561
That's fair.

689
00:35:05,395 --> 00:35:07,022
Kerama Island's gotta be beautiful.

690
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,023
Uninhabited island?

691
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:08,941
It's Zamami Island.

692
00:35:09,024 --> 00:35:10,984
Can you teach me how to make a highball?

693
00:35:11,068 --> 00:35:12,110
Sure.

694
00:35:12,194 --> 00:35:14,613
Went all the way to Naha,
took the ferry to Zamami

695
00:35:15,781 --> 00:35:17,115
and to an uninhabited island.

696
00:35:18,951 --> 00:35:20,244
Sorry about yesterday.

697
00:35:20,327 --> 00:35:21,495
Not at all.

698
00:35:21,578 --> 00:35:24,373
Honestly, thanks. I'm glad we talked.

699
00:35:24,456 --> 00:35:25,415
Drinks?

700
00:35:25,499 --> 00:35:26,375
I'll take a beer.

701
00:35:27,417 --> 00:35:29,586
Well, with the alcohol and everything…

702
00:35:29,670 --> 00:35:31,755
Oh no, me too.

703
00:35:31,839 --> 00:35:35,384
But don't hold back on my account.

704
00:35:35,467 --> 00:35:37,261
Let's both give it everything we've got.

705
00:35:38,220 --> 00:35:39,388
He's acting all jittery.

706
00:35:39,471 --> 00:35:41,390
He's 100% locked in on Yoko.

707
00:35:43,642 --> 00:35:46,019
It's great being at home.

708
00:35:46,520 --> 00:35:47,521
Yeah.

709
00:35:48,313 --> 00:35:49,314
So chill.

710
00:35:49,523 --> 00:35:51,024
Are they already living together?

711
00:35:51,817 --> 00:35:53,819
They're acting like newlyweds.

712
00:35:56,238 --> 00:35:59,575
For the rest of this vacation,

713
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:02,953
try imagining

714
00:36:04,788 --> 00:36:06,498
what it'd be like

715
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:09,793
if we got back together.

716
00:36:12,296 --> 00:36:13,964
Not right now,

717
00:36:14,715 --> 00:36:16,884
but picturing how life would look.

718
00:36:17,092 --> 00:36:18,510
I see.

719
00:36:19,344 --> 00:36:21,889
It might be hard to picture
if you put it like that.

720
00:36:21,972 --> 00:36:23,849
Oh, really?

721
00:36:23,932 --> 00:36:25,517
You mean picturing us back together?

722
00:36:25,601 --> 00:36:28,061
Not just getting back together,

723
00:36:28,228 --> 00:36:30,981
but picturing how we spend our time.

724
00:36:31,899 --> 00:36:35,027
Going out to eat,

725
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:38,030
and then

726
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:41,658
always just saying 'see you later'
and parting ways.

727
00:36:41,742 --> 00:36:45,996
I've been trapped in this
same repetitive cycle.

728
00:36:46,330 --> 00:36:47,873
I see.

729
00:36:48,832 --> 00:36:51,793
We spent Christmas together, too.

730
00:36:52,169 --> 00:36:54,129
I invited you to take a bath, right?

731
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:56,131
But then you came in like this.

732
00:36:57,174 --> 00:36:58,091
Yeah.

733
00:37:00,594 --> 00:37:03,972
When someone invites you to bathe together

734
00:37:04,306 --> 00:37:05,599
and you come in like that,

735
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:08,435
it's like, "Wait, what?"

736
00:37:11,730 --> 00:37:17,027
When I wanted you to step in closer,
you just wouldn't cross that line.

737
00:37:18,946 --> 00:37:20,447
Yeah, I understand.

738
00:37:20,572 --> 00:37:23,533
I was trying not to intrude too much
on your private life.

739
00:37:26,662 --> 00:37:27,955
Why?

740
00:37:28,956 --> 00:37:32,167
Yeah, you'd wonder why.

741
00:37:37,589 --> 00:37:42,970
There were times when she made it
totally obvious she was open to it,

742
00:37:43,053 --> 00:37:44,680
but I wouldn't bite.

743
00:37:46,056 --> 00:37:48,976
So she probably figured

744
00:37:49,059 --> 00:37:51,061
I wasn't interested anymore.

745
00:37:51,144 --> 00:37:53,647
But she's special to me.

746
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:59,236
She absolutely detests married guys

747
00:37:59,403 --> 00:38:04,324
hitting on her casually
or anything like that.

748
00:38:04,658 --> 00:38:07,744
So that's part of it.

749
00:38:07,828 --> 00:38:12,582
I figured she's the type
who gets hit on a lot.

750
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:15,669
So when I thought about that,

751
00:38:15,752 --> 00:38:20,132
I decided, "I want to be
the special one for her."

752
00:38:20,215 --> 00:38:22,551
"I want to build a genuine bond of trust."

753
00:38:22,634 --> 00:38:24,136
"So I need to stay disciplined."

754
00:38:24,219 --> 00:38:28,640
I refused to be the kind of guy who takes
advantage the second she shows an opening.

755
00:38:28,724 --> 00:38:31,143
That's all my strictness was about.

756
00:38:32,477 --> 00:38:35,564
I didn't mean anything weird by it.

757
00:38:36,356 --> 00:38:38,608
I see.

758
00:38:38,859 --> 00:38:40,819
He didn't want to be like the other guys.

759
00:38:40,986 --> 00:38:44,531
But honestly, doing nothing at all
might be even worse.

760
00:38:47,242 --> 00:38:50,746
I just wanted to be
uniquely special to you.

761
00:38:52,205 --> 00:38:53,081
But…

762
00:38:53,165 --> 00:38:56,209
So you thought it should've been
fine that way?

763
00:38:56,293 --> 00:39:00,338
But I think part of me
always deeply regretted that

764
00:39:00,422 --> 00:39:03,592
things could have turned out
completely differently.

765
00:39:05,552 --> 00:39:10,015
Still, I didn't want anyone else
taking away my spot

766
00:39:10,140 --> 00:39:12,726
as your special person,

767
00:39:13,602 --> 00:39:15,562
so I stayed strictly disciplined.

768
00:39:20,776 --> 00:39:22,652
Which means…

769
00:39:22,944 --> 00:39:26,073
your strictness actually worked.

770
00:39:26,490 --> 00:39:27,574
In a way.

771
00:39:27,657 --> 00:39:29,242
Why? Because you can't picture it?

772
00:39:29,785 --> 00:39:31,828
It's not that I can't picture it…

773
00:39:31,912 --> 00:39:33,747
it's because I haven't moved on yet.

774
00:39:37,584 --> 00:39:39,461
My "strictness" is…

775
00:39:39,544 --> 00:39:41,671
You did say, "Don't underestimate me."

776
00:39:41,755 --> 00:39:43,381
Yeah, it worked.

777
00:39:43,465 --> 00:39:45,258
But honestly,

778
00:39:45,842 --> 00:39:49,513
I just figured as long as you chose me
in the end, that's all that mattered.

779
00:39:49,679 --> 00:39:52,724
I was looking at this
across a 20- or 30-year span.

780
00:39:53,266 --> 00:39:56,686
That's how deeply I cared about you.

781
00:39:56,770 --> 00:39:59,022
I felt the exact same way.

782
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:01,858
I thought,
"Maybe I'll go marry someone else,

783
00:40:01,942 --> 00:40:05,695
get a divorce, and then
we'll finally end up together."

784
00:40:07,155 --> 00:40:09,991
I think we both had
that kind of long-term feeling.

785
00:40:10,325 --> 00:40:14,746
That's why… because that bond was

786
00:40:14,955 --> 00:40:16,957
always there inside me somewhere,

787
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:21,920
I could never fully walk away from you.

788
00:40:23,338 --> 00:40:25,799
Those two are on a whole different level.

789
00:40:25,882 --> 00:40:27,050
Incredible.

790
00:40:27,134 --> 00:40:29,553
That's on a massive scale.

791
00:40:29,636 --> 00:40:31,680
That's some intense romance.

792
00:40:31,763 --> 00:40:33,932
That's pure love right there. True love.

793
00:40:35,225 --> 00:40:39,271
Spending this kind of
peaceful time together

794
00:40:39,563 --> 00:40:42,566
makes me feel so happy,

795
00:40:44,651 --> 00:40:48,363
but part of me is still craving
that raw spark.

796
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:53,034
I always thought I wanted to
settle down with someone stable,

797
00:40:53,118 --> 00:40:57,122
but ideally

798
00:40:57,747 --> 00:40:59,708
after experiencing that

799
00:40:59,791 --> 00:41:01,751
initial rush and romantic thrill first.

800
00:41:01,835 --> 00:41:04,713
But with Daichi-san,
we skipped right to this

801
00:41:04,796 --> 00:41:08,258
comfortable, peaceful dynamic.

802
00:41:09,718 --> 00:41:13,847
Maybe if we had that physical intimacy,

803
00:41:14,181 --> 00:41:16,975
I could finally see him as a man, but…

804
00:41:18,059 --> 00:41:20,103
that's the part I'm struggling with.

805
00:41:21,813 --> 00:41:23,148
I want to change.

806
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:25,984
Myself.

807
00:41:26,693 --> 00:41:29,738
I want to actually experience
falling in love.

808
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:37,746
If I could,

809
00:41:39,331 --> 00:41:43,043
I'd want us to meet all over again
like it's the very first time.

810
00:41:44,211 --> 00:41:47,214
I actually get what she's saying.

811
00:41:48,423 --> 00:41:51,218
It's like wishing you could
un-see this whole movie.

812
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:53,386
Is this not a movie?

813
00:41:53,470 --> 00:41:55,013
No, they're real people!

814
00:41:55,555 --> 00:41:57,557
These people exist.

815
00:41:57,641 --> 00:41:59,309
They do?

816
00:42:01,228 --> 00:42:03,188
Realistically,

817
00:42:03,605 --> 00:42:06,233
trying to truly "start over"
from scratch is so hard.

818
00:42:06,316 --> 00:42:07,734
Yeah.

819
00:42:08,318 --> 00:42:11,738
So starting tomorrow,

820
00:42:12,614 --> 00:42:15,533
I want to try looking at you
like we just met.

821
00:42:15,617 --> 00:42:17,077
I see.

822
00:42:18,745 --> 00:42:20,538
That's even harder though, right?

823
00:42:21,039 --> 00:42:23,333
I'd probably say, "Nice to meet you."

824
00:42:25,085 --> 00:42:27,087
I just want a clean slate.

825
00:42:28,296 --> 00:42:29,297
Just for now.

826
00:42:29,381 --> 00:42:31,216
It's getting unexpectedly complicated.

827
00:42:31,925 --> 00:42:33,301
What's going to happen?

828
00:42:33,385 --> 00:42:35,512
There's barely any time left.

829
00:42:35,595 --> 00:42:36,721
Yeah, not much time.

830
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:42,644
What's going to happen to them?

831
00:42:45,146 --> 00:42:46,314
Let me put my stuff down.

832
00:42:46,398 --> 00:42:47,482
Right.

833
00:42:47,857 --> 00:42:51,027
I'll put my stuff down,
grab a coffee, and I'll be right back.

834
00:42:55,865 --> 00:42:58,034
Time for a little drink.

835
00:43:12,924 --> 00:43:15,010
Welcome back.

836
00:43:16,261 --> 00:43:17,679
Everyone's here.

837
00:43:18,513 --> 00:43:19,347
Nice.

838
00:43:19,431 --> 00:43:20,598
The wind is brutal.

839
00:43:20,682 --> 00:43:21,516
It's so cold.

840
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:22,434
Yeah.

841
00:43:22,851 --> 00:43:24,394
Where'd you guys go?

842
00:43:24,644 --> 00:43:25,520
Chatan.

843
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:26,813
Chatan?

844
00:43:27,188 --> 00:43:28,481
Chatan.

845
00:43:29,691 --> 00:43:30,817
Yeah.

846
00:43:31,609 --> 00:43:33,778
Did you guys eat dinner?

847
00:43:34,279 --> 00:43:35,280
We're good.

848
00:43:36,156 --> 00:43:37,365
It was good.

849
00:43:37,782 --> 00:43:39,826
What kind of look is that?

850
00:43:40,076 --> 00:43:42,495
Watching Ryo watching the two of them.

851
00:43:42,579 --> 00:43:44,331
Her expression is so complicated.

852
00:43:46,291 --> 00:43:47,500
You got tanned.

853
00:43:47,584 --> 00:43:49,419
He's wearing that saintly face.

854
00:43:49,961 --> 00:43:51,629
I'm glad Hikaru looks happy today.

855
00:43:51,796 --> 00:43:54,007
I'm always happy.

856
00:43:54,632 --> 00:43:56,384
I knew you'd say that.

857
00:43:56,468 --> 00:43:57,886
You knew he'd say that?

858
00:43:58,094 --> 00:44:00,013
He always says that.

859
00:44:00,096 --> 00:44:01,723
"I'm always happy."

860
00:44:02,974 --> 00:44:04,726
You love playing it cool, right?

861
00:44:04,976 --> 00:44:06,936
I never try to look cool.

862
00:44:07,020 --> 00:44:09,272
Really? So you're just naturally cool.

863
00:44:09,356 --> 00:44:10,774
What do you mean?

864
00:44:12,400 --> 00:44:13,234
Right?

865
00:44:14,194 --> 00:44:16,321
I felt like I was getting cornered,

866
00:44:16,404 --> 00:44:17,906
so I almost rebelled.

867
00:44:18,323 --> 00:44:19,824
Right?

868
00:44:19,949 --> 00:44:22,369
How many microscope slides
do you have left, Hikaru?

869
00:44:22,452 --> 00:44:23,828
Pretty much shattered by now.

870
00:44:25,663 --> 00:44:27,791
We need Kanako's song from yesterday.

871
00:44:27,957 --> 00:44:29,084
Should I sing it?

872
00:44:29,626 --> 00:44:31,586
What even is that?

873
00:44:32,003 --> 00:44:34,089
You don't know that iconic track?

874
00:44:35,173 --> 00:44:36,841
What song is this even?

875
00:44:37,842 --> 00:44:38,802
Last night.

876
00:44:38,885 --> 00:44:41,596
I just love this group of people so much.

877
00:44:41,888 --> 00:44:43,181
I love the living room crew.

878
00:44:43,348 --> 00:44:46,142
It was mostly Ryo-chin, Kanako, and me.

879
00:44:46,851 --> 00:44:48,144
We were basically a trio.

880
00:44:48,353 --> 00:44:50,563
You're like an idol.

881
00:44:51,022 --> 00:44:52,941
I wrote a song. Can I sing it now?

882
00:44:53,024 --> 00:44:54,359
Sure, go ahead.

883
00:44:54,442 --> 00:44:55,693
Can I sing it for real?

884
00:44:55,777 --> 00:44:56,861
Go for it.

885
00:44:56,945 --> 00:44:58,530
It's "Microscope Slide Heart."

886
00:44:58,613 --> 00:45:00,198
Microscope Slide Heart.

887
00:45:00,907 --> 00:45:03,576
You only use microscope slides
for science.

888
00:45:06,246 --> 00:45:12,085
Stacking 20,000 microscope slide hearts

889
00:45:12,460 --> 00:45:18,425
Every careless word shatters the glass.

890
00:45:18,508 --> 00:45:24,264
When we miss each other,
when the timing's off

891
00:45:24,347 --> 00:45:27,475
"What is my ex doing?"

892
00:45:27,559 --> 00:45:31,187
"What's on their mind?"

893
00:45:31,271 --> 00:45:35,442
I gotta know

894
00:45:37,068 --> 00:45:39,863
Microscope slide hearts

895
00:45:39,988 --> 00:45:43,074
How do you piece them back together?

896
00:45:43,158 --> 00:45:45,994
Is it a reunion

897
00:45:46,077 --> 00:45:49,205
or a brand new romance?

898
00:45:49,289 --> 00:45:51,624
Welcome to Love Transit.

899
00:45:51,749 --> 00:45:54,794
Welcome to Love Transit.

900
00:45:54,878 --> 00:45:57,505
Welcome to Love Transit.

901
00:45:57,589 --> 00:45:59,924
Someday it'll be shatterproof glass.

902
00:46:04,429 --> 00:46:05,680
What even is this?

903
00:46:05,763 --> 00:46:06,931
I want to cover this song.

904
00:46:07,682 --> 00:46:09,517
With Snow Man?

905
00:46:10,101 --> 00:46:11,269
Can you sing with me, Misato?

906
00:46:11,352 --> 00:46:12,479
Of course.

907
00:46:14,939 --> 00:46:16,024
Kaede.

908
00:46:16,274 --> 00:46:17,609
Is that Yoko-chan?

909
00:46:18,776 --> 00:46:23,948
A while ago, when I came into
the room to drop off coffee…

910
00:46:24,365 --> 00:46:27,327
I don't know, maybe he
panicked or something?

911
00:46:27,410 --> 00:46:31,414
He was like, "I want to go to your room,
I want to call you over."

912
00:46:31,498 --> 00:46:33,791
And I was like,
"What is this awkward vibe?"

913
00:46:33,875 --> 00:46:35,793
Oh, Hiroyoshi was freaking out?

914
00:46:35,877 --> 00:46:39,255
Let me drop my stuff off, grab a coffee,
and I'll be right back.

915
00:47:00,902 --> 00:47:02,153
Yoko-chan.

916
00:47:02,237 --> 00:47:05,240
Do you mind if I come over to
hang out in your room right now?

917
00:47:05,323 --> 00:47:06,491
My room?

918
00:47:08,576 --> 00:47:10,411
It's kind of cold out, so…

919
00:47:11,162 --> 00:47:12,497
Or my room…

920
00:47:12,705 --> 00:47:14,415
Let's stick to yours.

921
00:47:14,499 --> 00:47:15,333
Okay.

922
00:47:15,833 --> 00:47:17,043
I think he's got this

923
00:47:17,126 --> 00:47:19,754
underlying urge to keep her away
from Satoshi.

924
00:47:20,296 --> 00:47:22,382
He's totally on edge.

925
00:47:23,007 --> 00:47:24,384
Today was really fun.

926
00:47:24,467 --> 00:47:26,177
Thank you so much.

927
00:47:26,261 --> 00:47:27,887
Are you making coffee?

928
00:47:28,429 --> 00:47:29,764
What is it?

929
00:47:29,847 --> 00:47:31,432
Well…

930
00:47:33,810 --> 00:47:34,936
You know…

931
00:47:36,354 --> 00:47:38,273
you were saying

932
00:47:38,356 --> 00:47:42,485
how your romantic spark
just wasn't catching fire, right?

933
00:47:42,860 --> 00:47:45,905
When I thought about

934
00:47:46,197 --> 00:47:49,909
how there's a gap between us…

935
00:47:49,993 --> 00:47:53,871
well, not just love,
but a temperature difference…

936
00:47:54,622 --> 00:47:55,707
if you…

937
00:47:55,790 --> 00:47:58,293
genuinely want that intense,
burning kind of romance,

938
00:47:58,459 --> 00:48:01,045
then I mean, that's…

939
00:48:01,296 --> 00:48:02,589
I never said any of that.

940
00:48:02,672 --> 00:48:04,007
No you didn't. Sorry.

941
00:48:07,218 --> 00:48:08,803
She definitely didn't say that.

942
00:48:08,886 --> 00:48:10,513
Not at all.

943
00:48:11,389 --> 00:48:13,725
And honestly,
I felt like I really needed to

944
00:48:13,808 --> 00:48:15,977
learn from Satoshi's proactive energy,

945
00:48:16,269 --> 00:48:20,148
so when I saw you heading out,
I thought it was a good opportunity

946
00:48:20,565 --> 00:48:22,984
to spend some time together.

947
00:48:23,067 --> 00:48:24,319
Okay.

948
00:48:24,569 --> 00:48:25,945
I got it.

949
00:48:27,447 --> 00:48:28,740
Thank you.

950
00:48:29,532 --> 00:48:30,366
What is it?

951
00:48:30,450 --> 00:48:31,451
No, no, my bad.

952
00:48:33,077 --> 00:48:35,663
I also just wanted us to
spend some time together.

953
00:48:36,664 --> 00:48:40,043
I've been walking on eggshells and
holding back from calling you to my room.

954
00:48:40,126 --> 00:48:42,712
You're walking on eggshells like crazy.

955
00:48:43,171 --> 00:48:44,005
What do you mean?

956
00:48:44,088 --> 00:48:46,758
I feel like you're stressing
so much over how to treat me.

957
00:48:46,841 --> 00:48:48,301
Is everything okay?

958
00:48:48,384 --> 00:48:52,388
It's not even about walking on eggshells…

959
00:48:53,473 --> 00:48:56,184
well, maybe it is, I don't know.

960
00:48:56,267 --> 00:48:59,520
I'm just speaking straight from the heart.

961
00:48:59,729 --> 00:49:01,397
I think I look pathetic,

962
00:49:02,523 --> 00:49:03,650
honestly.

963
00:49:04,651 --> 00:49:07,028
Like I'm being super unmanly.

964
00:49:08,029 --> 00:49:10,073
I just want to try everything I can.

965
00:49:12,158 --> 00:49:16,537
Even if you're not thinking about
getting back together,

966
00:49:17,372 --> 00:49:21,793
I just want to do all I possibly can.

967
00:49:22,877 --> 00:49:24,003
And coming here

968
00:49:24,087 --> 00:49:27,757
made me realize how much you've been
accommodating me too.

969
00:49:28,424 --> 00:49:30,843
I'm not accommodating you.

970
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:32,553
Oh, really?

971
00:49:33,179 --> 00:49:35,098
I just said
I don't like being fussed over.

972
00:49:35,306 --> 00:49:37,725
And I just said
I wasn't fussing over you either.

973
00:49:44,982 --> 00:49:47,777
But I think I've always known that

974
00:49:47,860 --> 00:49:49,821
I'm more into you than you are into me.

975
00:49:52,198 --> 00:49:53,574
I…

976
00:49:53,741 --> 00:49:56,452
I want you to know I'm serious.

977
00:49:56,536 --> 00:49:57,870
Dead serious.

978
00:49:57,954 --> 00:49:58,830
I do feel that way.

979
00:49:59,580 --> 00:50:01,541
Okay, good.

980
00:50:01,916 --> 00:50:04,877
This is kind of my own personal issue.

981
00:50:04,961 --> 00:50:06,087
I see.

982
00:50:06,170 --> 00:50:07,213
From this point on.

983
00:50:08,589 --> 00:50:12,719
I don't think I've ever spent time
quite like this before.

984
00:50:14,053 --> 00:50:16,139
Right now, I kind of want to step outside.

985
00:50:16,222 --> 00:50:17,932
Do you want to head out, then?

986
00:50:18,015 --> 00:50:19,726
Sorry.

987
00:50:19,809 --> 00:50:21,436
They're just on
totally different wavelengths.

988
00:50:22,145 --> 00:50:26,107
He's trying his best, though.

989
00:50:26,190 --> 00:50:27,400
So dedicated.

990
00:50:27,734 --> 00:50:29,318
He's totally devoted.

991
00:50:29,402 --> 00:50:32,405
Better to voice how you feel
than keep it inside, right?

992
00:50:32,947 --> 00:50:36,534
Maybe someone with Satoshi-san's vibe
is actually a better match?

993
00:50:36,617 --> 00:50:37,618
Hard to say.

994
00:50:38,619 --> 00:50:41,289
I just couldn't stay in that room anymore.

995
00:50:41,831 --> 00:50:43,207
Such a waste.

996
00:50:43,291 --> 00:50:44,167
Yeah.

997
00:50:44,250 --> 00:50:46,753
He should've just ended it on a high note.

998
00:50:46,836 --> 00:50:49,005
The date was going so well.

999
00:50:50,131 --> 00:50:52,341
That was already enough.

1000
00:50:52,425 --> 00:50:55,011
That might've changed
your feelings all over again.

1001
00:50:55,094 --> 00:50:56,596
Exactly.

1002
00:50:56,679 --> 00:50:57,638
Such a waste.

1003
00:50:57,722 --> 00:50:59,098
Right.

1004
00:51:02,059 --> 00:51:03,561
Drinking alone.

1005
00:51:04,020 --> 00:51:05,438
Totally.

1006
00:51:08,649 --> 00:51:10,318
What is this?

1007
00:51:10,401 --> 00:51:11,277
IS THERE SOMEONE YOU'RE FEELING

1008
00:51:11,360 --> 00:51:12,195
A REAL SPARK FOR RIGHT NOW?

1009
00:51:12,278 --> 00:51:13,488
They got an email.

1010
00:51:16,449 --> 00:51:18,785
"Is there someone you're feeling

1011
00:51:18,868 --> 00:51:21,537
a real spark for right now?"

1012
00:51:21,621 --> 00:51:25,333
So they're sending an email to
someone they have a spark for.

1013
00:51:25,458 --> 00:51:28,836
"If there is one,
please send them a message."

1014
00:51:29,378 --> 00:51:32,089
Is this a spark?

1015
00:51:32,173 --> 00:51:36,385
The anonymous email system
has finally been triggered.

1016
00:51:36,469 --> 00:51:39,639
"You can't receive anything unless
you complete your own transmission."

1017
00:51:39,722 --> 00:51:42,683
"You can't wait to see what
the other person does before sending."

1018
00:51:42,767 --> 00:51:46,604
"The only thing disclosed is
whether it came from your X or not."

1019
00:51:46,687 --> 00:51:48,606
And the crucial instruction is that

1020
00:51:48,689 --> 00:51:51,692
you have to send a message
if there is someone.

1021
00:51:51,776 --> 00:51:55,279
Meaning, if there's no one
you're feeling a spark for,

1022
00:51:55,363 --> 00:51:57,657
you don't have to send anything.

1023
00:51:58,324 --> 00:51:59,617
Right.

1024
00:52:23,182 --> 00:52:25,017
HIROYOSHI

1025
00:52:29,021 --> 00:52:29,897
0

1026
00:52:31,607 --> 00:52:33,317
Nothing for Hiroyoshi!

1027
00:52:33,651 --> 00:52:36,028
YOUR X DIDN'T CHOOSE YOU

1028
00:52:39,949 --> 00:52:41,617
Hiroyoshi didn't get one.

1029
00:52:41,701 --> 00:52:44,662
That means Yoko sent hers to Satoshi?

1030
00:52:44,745 --> 00:52:46,038
Did she send it to Satoshi?

1031
00:52:46,247 --> 00:52:48,207
Did she even send it to anyone?

1032
00:52:48,291 --> 00:52:50,501
True.

1033
00:53:02,763 --> 00:53:04,098
HIKARU

1034
00:53:04,557 --> 00:53:07,018
Could this be mutual?

1035
00:53:07,101 --> 00:53:09,896
I'd like to think it's mutual…

1036
00:53:11,147 --> 00:53:11,981
0

1037
00:53:15,443 --> 00:53:16,569
YOUR X DIDN'T CHOOSE YOU

1038
00:53:18,696 --> 00:53:20,031
Then…

1039
00:53:20,114 --> 00:53:21,407
Ryo-chan?

1040
00:53:23,242 --> 00:53:24,410
Alright.

1041
00:53:27,204 --> 00:53:29,206
Thanks. That cheered me up.

1042
00:53:29,290 --> 00:53:30,374
Thanks, Kanako.

1043
00:53:32,960 --> 00:53:35,713
Good night.

1044
00:53:35,922 --> 00:53:37,298
Good night.

1045
00:53:40,343 --> 00:53:41,928
Wanna hang out tomorrow?

1046
00:53:42,011 --> 00:53:42,929
Sure.

1047
00:53:43,012 --> 00:53:44,055
Oh?

1048
00:53:44,388 --> 00:53:46,724
I have work from 9 to 11.

1049
00:53:46,807 --> 00:53:49,310
Oh, is that so? Is 12 okay?

1050
00:53:49,393 --> 00:53:50,937
Okay.

1051
00:53:51,646 --> 00:53:52,939
Thanks.

1052
00:53:53,522 --> 00:53:55,358
Mao asked him out.

1053
00:53:55,441 --> 00:53:56,567
She asked Ryo-chan out.

1054
00:54:01,072 --> 00:54:04,450
I never thought
I'd get asked out on a date,

1055
00:54:04,825 --> 00:54:07,078
so I'm just really happy.

1056
00:54:08,329 --> 00:54:12,500
She's so lovely when she's smiling.

1057
00:54:13,417 --> 00:54:15,878
Saying it out loud makes me
kind of embarrassed, though.

1058
00:54:22,635 --> 00:54:24,971
So Mao didn't send one to anyone?

1059
00:54:25,054 --> 00:54:25,972
But then again,

1060
00:54:26,055 --> 00:54:28,849
Mao did ask Ryo out at the very end.

1061
00:54:29,308 --> 00:54:31,394
We don't know what's going to happen.

1062
00:54:31,477 --> 00:54:35,147
In the '35+ season, you've got people

1063
00:54:35,272 --> 00:54:39,110
whose relationships have gone way past
that initial heart-fluttering spark.

1064
00:54:39,193 --> 00:54:42,863
Even if they're getting back together,
it might not feel like a 'spark'.

1065
00:54:42,947 --> 00:54:44,448
They might've gotten caught up

1066
00:54:44,532 --> 00:54:46,701
on the word 'spark'
and didn't send anything.

1067
00:54:46,784 --> 00:54:48,619
The definition of 'spark'.

1068
00:54:48,703 --> 00:54:50,788
The word 'spark' is…

1069
00:54:50,871 --> 00:54:54,417
And with time running out,

1070
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:55,876
everyone's choices

1071
00:54:55,960 --> 00:54:58,838
are starting to feel a lot more real.

1072
00:54:58,921 --> 00:55:03,342
What stood out to me was
Kaede-san and Daichi-san.

1073
00:55:03,426 --> 00:55:06,804
Just when you'd think
they're cruising along smoothly,

1074
00:55:07,096 --> 00:55:09,265
it almost felt like

1075
00:55:09,348 --> 00:55:12,184
Kaede-san was indirectly

1076
00:55:12,727 --> 00:55:14,812
asking him to hit the brakes.

1077
00:55:14,895 --> 00:55:15,980
The microscope slide, huh.

1078
00:55:16,063 --> 00:55:18,315
I could totally see the microscope slide.

1079
00:55:18,399 --> 00:55:20,735
That was great though.

1080
00:55:20,818 --> 00:55:23,112
I wonder how bored they were
in the living room.

1081
00:55:30,995 --> 00:55:32,538
She's displaying it.

1082
00:55:39,587 --> 00:55:41,464
What should I do?

1083
00:55:45,051 --> 00:55:46,385
I have no idea.

1084
00:55:47,344 --> 00:55:49,638
He's totally lost.

1085
00:55:59,607 --> 00:56:01,192
I woke up

1086
00:56:01,275 --> 00:56:03,736
like several times,

1087
00:56:03,819 --> 00:56:06,155
boiled some water and took a bath.

1088
00:56:06,238 --> 00:56:08,074
Is Mao-chan gonna be around all day today?

1089
00:56:08,157 --> 00:56:08,991
I have no idea.

1090
00:56:09,075 --> 00:56:09,909
Okay.

1091
00:56:11,368 --> 00:56:12,870
I don't know either.

1092
00:56:14,121 --> 00:56:15,247
I only know about myself.

1093
00:56:15,331 --> 00:56:16,791
Oh, yeah?

1094
00:56:18,167 --> 00:56:19,960
Good morning.

1095
00:56:20,336 --> 00:56:21,670
Starting a bit late today?

1096
00:56:21,754 --> 00:56:23,089
Work.

1097
00:56:24,048 --> 00:56:26,550
Is everyone here?

1098
00:56:26,634 --> 00:56:27,802
Is nobody going on a date?

1099
00:56:27,885 --> 00:56:29,386
Not me.

1100
00:56:29,470 --> 00:56:31,972
Being wishy-washy.

1101
00:56:32,264 --> 00:56:33,265
I'm heading out.

1102
00:56:33,349 --> 00:56:35,351
Have fun!

1103
00:56:36,477 --> 00:56:37,853
So cute.

1104
00:56:37,937 --> 00:56:40,147
I wonder where she's going.

1105
00:56:42,858 --> 00:56:44,110
Not even a glance.

1106
00:56:55,454 --> 00:56:56,705
Are you feeling melancholic?

1107
00:56:57,039 --> 00:56:58,040
Yes.

1108
00:56:58,124 --> 00:57:00,918
All by yourself?

1109
00:57:01,710 --> 00:57:02,545
Heading out?

1110
00:57:02,628 --> 00:57:03,504
Heading out.

1111
00:57:03,587 --> 00:57:04,880
Oh, seriously?

1112
00:57:04,964 --> 00:57:06,132
Going out, yeah.

1113
00:57:06,215 --> 00:57:07,049
That's right.

1114
00:57:07,133 --> 00:57:08,300
Nice.

1115
00:57:08,384 --> 00:57:12,388
I just figured I'd try to enjoy myself.

1116
00:57:15,099 --> 00:57:19,854
I'm keeping that kind of positive mindset.

1117
00:57:21,689 --> 00:57:23,190
He's here.

1118
00:57:23,274 --> 00:57:24,900
Let's roll, shall we?

1119
00:57:24,984 --> 00:57:26,819
Thanks.

1120
00:57:26,902 --> 00:57:27,736
Have fun.

1121
00:57:27,820 --> 00:57:28,821
Thanks.

1122
00:57:28,904 --> 00:57:30,656
Catch you later.

1123
00:57:30,739 --> 00:57:31,907
See ya.

1124
00:57:34,577 --> 00:57:36,245
How was work?

1125
00:57:36,328 --> 00:57:37,746
I had meetings the whole time.

1126
00:57:37,830 --> 00:57:39,248
Oh, really?

1127
00:57:40,124 --> 00:57:41,709
Is she going with Hikaru?

1128
00:57:42,001 --> 00:57:44,211
No, with Ryo.

1129
00:57:44,295 --> 00:57:47,173
Really? I see.

1130
00:57:47,298 --> 00:57:49,258
I knew he would do that.

1131
00:57:49,341 --> 00:57:51,010
Ryo-chan's pretty cool

1132
00:57:51,135 --> 00:57:52,261
for making the move.

1133
00:57:52,344 --> 00:57:53,179
Yeah.

1134
00:57:53,262 --> 00:57:56,223
What if Mao's the one who asked him out?

1135
00:57:56,849 --> 00:57:58,809
Oh right, Mao did say she liked Ryo-chan.

1136
00:57:58,893 --> 00:58:00,936
Really? Then maybe…

1137
00:58:01,020 --> 00:58:02,771
Are their feelings actually mutual?

1138
00:58:03,355 --> 00:58:05,649
Wait, hold on. Seriously?

1139
00:58:06,442 --> 00:58:07,651
I don't know.

1140
00:58:08,652 --> 00:58:10,988
Well, if that's the case,
I'm rooting for them.

1141
00:58:12,198 --> 00:58:15,075
Mao's worked so hard up until now.

1142
00:58:15,159 --> 00:58:17,828
For over ten years.

1143
00:58:19,830 --> 00:58:21,582
True, true.

1144
00:58:23,292 --> 00:58:24,543
Alright.

1145
00:58:26,879 --> 00:58:28,088
The ceiling's so low.

1146
00:58:28,172 --> 00:58:29,048
It is.

1147
00:58:29,673 --> 00:58:32,092
Where's… this car is way too new.

1148
00:58:32,176 --> 00:58:34,887
I have no idea where
the gas pedal even is.

1149
00:58:36,347 --> 00:58:37,306
Here we go!

1150
00:58:37,389 --> 00:58:38,766
Let's do this.

1151
00:58:39,391 --> 00:58:40,643
So quiet.

1152
00:58:40,726 --> 00:58:44,063
My car makes a big rumbling sound.

1153
00:58:45,898 --> 00:58:47,691
Do you ever go for drives?

1154
00:58:47,775 --> 00:58:51,779
I'd love to if I had a car,

1155
00:58:51,862 --> 00:58:54,406
but my car's gone now.

1156
00:58:55,074 --> 00:58:56,200
Because it got sold.

1157
00:58:56,492 --> 00:58:58,035
So sad.

1158
00:58:58,702 --> 00:59:00,287
No car because it got sold…

1159
00:59:05,334 --> 00:59:06,752
I just tried

1160
00:59:07,503 --> 00:59:09,129
adjusting the seat angle.

1161
00:59:09,213 --> 00:59:10,047
Really?

1162
00:59:11,090 --> 00:59:12,466
It was a little forward.

1163
00:59:12,549 --> 00:59:14,760
This isn't a car you drive

1164
00:59:14,843 --> 00:59:17,263
all stiff and nervous
with a ten-and-two grip.

1165
00:59:17,346 --> 00:59:19,723
I should've realized that sooner.

1166
00:59:21,225 --> 00:59:22,851
So colorful. Okinawa.

1167
00:59:23,811 --> 00:59:24,728
So cute.

1168
00:59:24,812 --> 00:59:25,896
Okay.

1169
00:59:29,900 --> 00:59:30,985
I like the "Okina".

1170
00:59:31,068 --> 00:59:31,902
It's "Okina".

1171
00:59:33,112 --> 00:59:34,613
This thing has some speed!

1172
00:59:36,865 --> 00:59:38,200
So fast.

1173
00:59:39,994 --> 00:59:41,620
Oh, it's so pretty! Super pretty!

1174
00:59:41,829 --> 00:59:43,831
One of those where you can see underwater.

1175
00:59:43,914 --> 00:59:45,499
Look. There.

1176
00:59:45,582 --> 00:59:47,042
I see it!

1177
00:59:47,793 --> 00:59:49,086
Wow.

1178
00:59:49,169 --> 00:59:50,254
I could catch one.

1179
00:59:50,337 --> 00:59:51,422
Let's do it.

1180
00:59:51,922 --> 00:59:53,048
Dinner for tonight.

1181
00:59:53,132 --> 00:59:54,717
It will be our dinner.

1182
00:59:56,218 --> 00:59:57,219
Look, look.

1183
00:59:57,303 --> 00:59:59,888
That scared me.

1184
01:00:00,222 --> 01:00:01,724
Seriously gave me a fright.

1185
01:00:01,807 --> 01:00:03,267
Looks like they're having fun.

1186
01:00:03,350 --> 01:00:06,103
It gives off a completely different vibe
compared to Hikaru.

1187
01:00:09,440 --> 01:00:10,441
Wait…

1188
01:00:14,778 --> 01:00:15,988
This is hilarious.

1189
01:00:20,826 --> 01:00:22,494
What is he doing?

1190
01:00:22,786 --> 01:00:23,704
Eating lunch alone.

1191
01:00:23,787 --> 01:00:25,205
He's eating alone.

1192
01:00:27,499 --> 01:00:29,251
Looks like we can't hit the pool today.

1193
01:00:29,335 --> 01:00:30,711
It's warm over here.

1194
01:00:30,794 --> 01:00:31,628
Oh, true.

1195
01:00:31,712 --> 01:00:33,297
Heated water, a Jacuzzi.

1196
01:00:35,966 --> 01:00:38,010
He's looking kind of down.

1197
01:00:41,180 --> 01:00:42,639
Kanao, did you go to the beach?

1198
01:00:42,723 --> 01:00:43,599
No, I want to.

1199
01:00:43,682 --> 01:00:44,516
Let's go, then.

1200
01:00:44,600 --> 01:00:45,809
Oh?

1201
01:00:45,893 --> 01:00:46,810
Let's check it out.

1202
01:00:46,894 --> 01:00:47,728
Go on ahead.

1203
01:00:47,811 --> 01:00:48,771
Excuse us.

1204
01:00:48,854 --> 01:00:49,980
Go ahead.

1205
01:00:50,356 --> 01:00:51,565
I wanted to see the beach.

1206
01:00:51,648 --> 01:00:52,566
Yay.

1207
01:00:52,649 --> 01:00:55,569
Satoshi asking Kanako out is pretty rare.

1208
01:00:55,652 --> 01:00:56,904
Wonder what's going on.

1209
01:00:56,987 --> 01:00:59,656
I just wanted to talk for a bit.

1210
01:00:59,740 --> 01:01:01,700
Okay. What's up?

1211
01:01:02,076 --> 01:01:04,036
Yesterday, you know…

1212
01:01:04,119 --> 01:01:07,539
you were really open and honest with me

1213
01:01:07,790 --> 01:01:09,500
at the cafe.

1214
01:01:10,125 --> 01:01:13,837
And my response to that…

1215
01:01:14,129 --> 01:01:16,423
I didn't really handle it properly.

1216
01:01:17,383 --> 01:01:19,760
I've spent all night

1217
01:01:19,927 --> 01:01:22,554
regretting that.

1218
01:01:22,638 --> 01:01:25,599
So… kind of as a follow-up to that,

1219
01:01:25,766 --> 01:01:28,727
I wanted to tell you properly.

1220
01:01:30,312 --> 01:01:34,566
I thought we were dating.

1221
01:01:34,775 --> 01:01:37,736
But you felt like we weren't.

1222
01:01:38,320 --> 01:01:41,990
Honestly, that came as a bit of a shock.

1223
01:01:42,825 --> 01:01:44,451
It felt like

1224
01:01:44,535 --> 01:01:49,206
a total factory reset on my emotions.

1225
01:01:51,041 --> 01:01:55,421
Like, if that was your stance,

1226
01:01:55,504 --> 01:01:59,133
then fine, screw it. To put it simply.

1227
01:01:59,216 --> 01:02:02,302
Giving into that kind of vibe

1228
01:02:03,345 --> 01:02:06,932
really showed how immature
and childish I was being.

1229
01:02:07,349 --> 01:02:11,645
I should've talked
just between the two of us first,

1230
01:02:11,937 --> 01:02:16,150
and just said what was
actually on my mind.

1231
01:02:17,693 --> 01:02:19,611
What I really should've done

1232
01:02:19,695 --> 01:02:22,364
above all else was
put myself in your shoes.

1233
01:02:23,157 --> 01:02:27,077
He actually digested all that
and really came around.

1234
01:02:27,661 --> 01:02:31,790
To be honest, when it comes to love
or this whole hocance deal,

1235
01:02:31,874 --> 01:02:35,794
I've never even used the phrase

1236
01:02:35,961 --> 01:02:38,255
"facing someone head-on."

1237
01:02:40,466 --> 01:02:42,468
Like, "What does that even mean?"

1238
01:02:44,553 --> 01:02:45,929
To be honest.

1239
01:02:46,138 --> 01:02:49,600
I was just riding on their good nature

1240
01:02:49,683 --> 01:02:52,186
the whole time. Pure luck, really.

1241
01:02:52,352 --> 01:02:54,897
That's how I felt yesterday.

1242
01:02:55,647 --> 01:02:57,024
I see.

1243
01:02:58,317 --> 01:03:01,695
If I was ever gonna use
that word for real,

1244
01:03:02,112 --> 01:03:04,948
it had to be with you first…

1245
01:03:12,664 --> 01:03:13,749
Oh, sorry.

1246
01:03:14,583 --> 01:03:16,084
Are you okay?

1247
01:03:17,085 --> 01:03:18,587
Sorry, I'm good.

1248
01:03:18,670 --> 01:03:20,756
I should've stepped up
and faced you head-on.

1249
01:03:24,259 --> 01:03:27,054
Instead, I chickened out,

1250
01:03:27,137 --> 01:03:31,350
tried to make excuses for my own bullshit,

1251
01:03:31,433 --> 01:03:34,520
and ended up taking it out

1252
01:03:34,603 --> 01:03:36,355
on you a lot.

1253
01:03:37,856 --> 01:03:39,608
So, I'm really sorry.

1254
01:03:43,654 --> 01:03:47,449
That's what I should've
told you first yesterday,

1255
01:03:47,533 --> 01:03:49,326
and I needed to say it today.

1256
01:03:51,495 --> 01:03:53,830
So you actually sat with it.

1257
01:03:57,876 --> 01:04:00,504
You're doing way better at
facing people than yesterday.

1258
01:04:02,923 --> 01:04:03,840
A first for me.

1259
01:04:03,924 --> 01:04:04,967
Oh yeah?

1260
01:04:07,135 --> 01:04:09,846
In his own way,
he's pushing himself so hard right now.

1261
01:04:09,930 --> 01:04:12,182
I wanted to actually hear him out,

1262
01:04:13,016 --> 01:04:15,227
and you could see

1263
01:04:15,310 --> 01:04:17,771
how much he grew overnight.

1264
01:04:17,854 --> 01:04:19,022
Knowing that

1265
01:04:19,106 --> 01:04:22,359
what I said got through to him
and triggered that change made me happy.

1266
01:04:22,442 --> 01:04:23,777
That's insane growth.

1267
01:04:23,860 --> 01:04:26,863
Since we're on this hocance together,

1268
01:04:27,281 --> 01:04:29,866
I really wanted him to walk away
having learned something,

1269
01:04:29,950 --> 01:04:33,954
just like I want to leave here
a better person too.

1270
01:04:34,037 --> 01:04:37,749
He actually opened up about
where his head's at,

1271
01:04:37,833 --> 01:04:39,585
so it was a really good talk.

1272
01:04:39,876 --> 01:04:41,420
Huge weight off my chest.

1273
01:04:42,671 --> 01:04:45,007
Glad to hear
things shifted for the better.

1274
01:04:48,677 --> 01:04:49,845
Thank you.

1275
01:04:49,928 --> 01:04:52,848
A real apology changes everything.

1276
01:04:56,935 --> 01:04:58,895
Will you sing for me one more time?

1277
01:04:58,979 --> 01:05:00,147
No way in hell.

1278
01:05:00,230 --> 01:05:01,315
Seriously?

1279
01:05:01,773 --> 01:05:03,066
He actually liked it!

1280
01:05:03,150 --> 01:05:04,234
Freaking hilarious.

1281
01:05:04,318 --> 01:05:06,653
So he liked that song, too.

1282
01:05:06,737 --> 01:05:09,448
Nice, Satoshi.

1283
01:05:09,531 --> 01:05:11,742
I think Satoshi is a funny guy, too.

1284
01:05:12,075 --> 01:05:13,619
When did you write that?

1285
01:05:13,702 --> 01:05:15,537
I was so bored at night,

1286
01:05:15,621 --> 01:05:17,706
staring at the ceiling and
thinking like crazy.

1287
01:05:19,124 --> 01:05:20,792
But hey, that's just who I am.

1288
01:05:21,793 --> 01:05:25,172
If it gave everyone a little boost,
then awesome.

1289
01:05:25,255 --> 01:05:27,966
The girls even brought it up
again this morning.

1290
01:05:28,342 --> 01:05:30,510
Honestly, it gave me a massive push too.

1291
01:05:31,303 --> 01:05:32,804
After inspiring everyone like that,

1292
01:05:32,888 --> 01:05:34,765
I ended up with zero messages last night.

1293
01:05:37,309 --> 01:05:38,685
I just tapped "like".

1294
01:05:40,187 --> 01:05:42,939
"Your ex didn't choose you." "Thumbs up!"

1295
01:05:44,066 --> 01:05:46,109
These two are so funny together.

1296
01:05:46,193 --> 01:05:47,778
Satoshi didn't send one to her!

1297
01:05:52,908 --> 01:05:54,326
You usually sit on the left or right?

1298
01:05:54,409 --> 01:05:56,161
Either's fine.

1299
01:05:56,244 --> 01:05:57,162
Or the back?

1300
01:05:57,245 --> 01:06:00,123
Wait, you mean the back seat?
No, I'm riding shotgun.

1301
01:06:00,207 --> 01:06:03,251
This is a pretty rare pairing too.

1302
01:06:03,460 --> 01:06:05,087
But purely for advice not romance.

1303
01:06:05,170 --> 01:06:06,296
Right.

1304
01:06:07,506 --> 01:06:09,049
Where can I throw this out?

1305
01:06:09,466 --> 01:06:11,718
That was awesome.

1306
01:06:11,802 --> 01:06:13,011
Will you sing the song?

1307
01:06:13,095 --> 01:06:14,137
I will.

1308
01:06:15,472 --> 01:06:16,306
Good night.

1309
01:06:16,390 --> 01:06:17,599
Good night, Kanako.

1310
01:06:18,308 --> 01:06:19,559
That was a great song.

1311
01:06:19,976 --> 01:06:21,103
Wanna go on a date tomorrow?

1312
01:06:21,812 --> 01:06:24,356
Sounds like a plan.

1313
01:06:24,439 --> 01:06:26,066
12:15.

1314
01:06:26,149 --> 01:06:27,275
Got it.

1315
01:06:28,151 --> 01:06:30,570
Throughout the hocance,

1316
01:06:30,654 --> 01:06:33,156
I felt like he got me
better than anyone else

1317
01:06:33,240 --> 01:06:35,409
and we just clicked.

1318
01:06:35,992 --> 01:06:38,829
I was so sure I wanted
one last date with him.

1319
01:06:39,121 --> 01:06:41,331
Ever since that memorable date we went on,

1320
01:06:42,791 --> 01:06:45,836
he's been in the back of
my mind somewhere.

1321
01:06:46,086 --> 01:06:48,255
Out of those five guys,

1322
01:06:49,214 --> 01:06:51,842
I always felt someone like Hika-chan

1323
01:06:51,925 --> 01:06:53,635
would be the best fit for me.

1324
01:06:53,719 --> 01:06:56,930
After all the heavy stuff,
there's nothing left but good vibes.

1325
01:06:58,140 --> 01:07:00,475
Mentally, I'm way more relaxed now

1326
01:07:00,559 --> 01:07:02,144
than I was during the hocance.

1327
01:07:02,227 --> 01:07:03,353
I'm having a blast.

1328
01:07:03,437 --> 01:07:04,312
That's great.

1329
01:07:04,563 --> 01:07:07,816
Things are really shaking up
now that they're on vacation.

1330
01:07:08,525 --> 01:07:09,901
Taking some unexpected turns.

1331
01:07:09,985 --> 01:07:11,403
Must be that Okinawa magic.

1332
01:07:11,570 --> 01:07:13,113
Okinawa really works wonders.

1333
01:07:13,196 --> 01:07:14,740
I wanna go to Okinawa so bad.

1334
01:07:16,783 --> 01:07:19,035
My hair got all sticky earlier.

1335
01:07:19,119 --> 01:07:21,580
From the ocean salt?

1336
01:07:21,913 --> 01:07:22,748
Didn't yours?

1337
01:07:22,831 --> 01:07:24,082
I did too.

1338
01:07:24,166 --> 01:07:25,917
I was so sticky.

1339
01:07:26,835 --> 01:07:29,212
I was way too busy curling my hair.

1340
01:07:29,296 --> 01:07:31,423
Curling it, blowing it out…

1341
01:07:31,506 --> 01:07:34,968
I had it up in a bun first,
then pulled it down.

1342
01:07:35,051 --> 01:07:37,512
What was wrong with the bun?

1343
01:07:38,638 --> 01:07:40,056
Oh, so you preferred the bun?

1344
01:07:40,140 --> 01:07:40,974
No, no.

1345
01:07:42,184 --> 01:07:43,351
It's just fresh seeing you like that.

1346
01:07:43,435 --> 01:07:44,644
Fresh?

1347
01:07:44,728 --> 01:07:46,438
"Preferred the bun?"

1348
01:07:47,314 --> 01:07:49,649
Everyone's got their own thing.

1349
01:07:49,733 --> 01:07:52,486
I looked at my shoes earlier.
Totally full of sand.

1350
01:07:52,569 --> 01:07:54,070
I still have some.

1351
01:07:54,154 --> 01:07:55,071
They're cute.

1352
01:07:55,155 --> 01:07:56,364
Cute, right?

1353
01:07:58,575 --> 01:08:00,744
How about you, Kae-chan?

1354
01:08:02,037 --> 01:08:04,206
I couldn't send a message.

1355
01:08:04,289 --> 01:08:05,499
I see.

1356
01:08:05,874 --> 01:08:07,876
She couldn't send one to Daichi.

1357
01:08:07,959 --> 01:08:09,127
Wait, what, bad Wi-Fi?

1358
01:08:09,211 --> 01:08:10,170
It's not a Wi-Fi thing.

1359
01:08:10,253 --> 01:08:12,005
She doesn't mean it literally.

1360
01:08:12,088 --> 01:08:14,424
She just couldn't bring herself to do it.

1361
01:08:14,508 --> 01:08:15,884
It's not a signal issue.

1362
01:08:15,967 --> 01:08:17,844
I'm sorry.

1363
01:08:18,345 --> 01:08:19,596
Yeah, I get it.

1364
01:08:19,679 --> 01:08:22,098
I haven't gotten a single message either.

1365
01:08:29,022 --> 01:08:31,149
All I can say is, "yes, yes."

1366
01:08:36,780 --> 01:08:38,740
Gonna go chat with her for a sec.

1367
01:08:38,990 --> 01:08:40,826
Excuse me.

1368
01:08:40,909 --> 01:08:42,118
Scoot over a bit then.

1369
01:08:42,202 --> 01:08:43,703
Excuse me.

1370
01:08:43,787 --> 01:08:44,788
Cheers.

1371
01:08:44,871 --> 01:08:46,164
Where is Dai-chan?

1372
01:08:46,248 --> 01:08:47,290
I think he's asleep.

1373
01:08:47,374 --> 01:08:48,500
Asleep?

1374
01:08:53,296 --> 01:08:55,048
Well, well…

1375
01:08:57,217 --> 01:08:58,468
Do you actually like her?

1376
01:08:58,552 --> 01:09:00,428
I don't even know anymore.

1377
01:09:01,096 --> 01:09:02,722
"I don't even know"?

1378
01:09:02,806 --> 01:09:05,517
She told me I like chasing her.

1379
01:09:05,600 --> 01:09:07,227
And yeah, I've been doing all the chasing,

1380
01:09:07,310 --> 01:09:09,354
thinking it's just 'cause I liked her.

1381
01:09:09,729 --> 01:09:12,357
But this time, I've chased her this hard,

1382
01:09:13,191 --> 01:09:16,653
barely got any texts back,

1383
01:09:16,736 --> 01:09:18,780
then we finally had a date yesterday

1384
01:09:19,406 --> 01:09:23,410
and it felt like things were
finally back to normal.

1385
01:09:23,493 --> 01:09:25,245
Might as well hit the hot tub, right?

1386
01:09:26,454 --> 01:09:27,873
We haven't drunk that much yet.

1387
01:09:27,956 --> 01:09:29,207
Yeah, let's do that.

1388
01:09:29,291 --> 01:09:30,750
Go get changed.

1389
01:09:30,834 --> 01:09:32,836
Go on, Kaede.

1390
01:09:38,383 --> 01:09:39,926
Oji!

1391
01:10:07,537 --> 01:10:09,414
Stunning.

1392
01:10:10,165 --> 01:10:11,499
You're here.

1393
01:10:12,083 --> 01:10:13,501
I was just doing laps.

1394
01:10:13,585 --> 01:10:14,794
Isn't it cold?

1395
01:10:15,253 --> 01:10:16,755
Not at all.

1396
01:10:17,339 --> 01:10:18,465
Just zooming all around.

1397
01:10:18,548 --> 01:10:19,424
Seriously?

1398
01:10:21,843 --> 01:10:23,511
Oh wow.

1399
01:10:23,803 --> 01:10:26,473
Look at this gorgeous lady!

1400
01:10:27,515 --> 01:10:30,936
Hiro-san waltzing right in with her
like it's nothing.

1401
01:10:31,311 --> 01:10:34,105
What is that guy's deal?

1402
01:10:34,189 --> 01:10:35,857
Oh, so she cares.

1403
01:10:35,941 --> 01:10:37,651
She still has those feelings.

1404
01:10:37,734 --> 01:10:40,612
Deep down, maybe everyone feels
a bit possessive

1405
01:10:40,862 --> 01:10:43,865
when it comes to their ex.

1406
01:10:44,240 --> 01:10:45,075
Are you jealous?

1407
01:10:45,283 --> 01:10:46,117
It's not jealousy.

1408
01:10:47,661 --> 01:10:49,788
Not jealousy.

1409
01:10:50,080 --> 01:10:51,539
Definitely not jealousy.

1410
01:10:54,376 --> 01:10:56,628
Kaede's in the hot tub!

1411
01:10:59,923 --> 01:11:01,466
What were we talking about again?

1412
01:11:01,967 --> 01:11:02,801
Feelings?

1413
01:11:02,884 --> 01:11:04,427
That's right.

1414
01:11:05,595 --> 01:11:07,180
Like yesterday too…

1415
01:11:07,263 --> 01:11:10,433
I told her, "Wanna head to my room?
Or you can come on over."

1416
01:11:10,517 --> 01:11:12,310
When she came in, she was acting

1417
01:11:12,394 --> 01:11:14,145
so walled off I almost wondered

1418
01:11:14,229 --> 01:11:15,563
if she hated me.

1419
01:11:16,022 --> 01:11:17,023
Like, rejection?

1420
01:11:17,107 --> 01:11:22,362
Pretty close. After that, I was like,
"Yeah, this is not gonna work."

1421
01:11:22,445 --> 01:11:24,656
Maybe as friends, sure,

1422
01:11:24,739 --> 01:11:27,075
but romance? Zero chance moving forward.

1423
01:11:28,952 --> 01:11:30,036
It's done.

1424
01:11:31,037 --> 01:11:31,871
You thought so?

1425
01:11:31,955 --> 01:11:32,789
Yeah.

1426
01:11:33,957 --> 01:11:36,626
I know that look in her eyes…

1427
01:11:37,419 --> 01:11:39,212
that honeymoon spark

1428
01:11:39,295 --> 01:11:41,965
when someone's totally head over heels?

1429
01:11:42,257 --> 01:11:44,634
I just feel like that look's
never coming back.

1430
01:11:44,884 --> 01:11:46,136
You felt that way from the beginning?

1431
01:11:46,219 --> 01:11:47,053
Yeah.

1432
01:11:47,137 --> 01:11:51,766
So, is me chasing after her
actually gonna make anyone happy?

1433
01:11:52,350 --> 01:11:56,813
Even if she took me back out of pity,

1434
01:11:56,896 --> 01:11:59,232
it wouldn't be because
she fell for me again.

1435
01:11:59,441 --> 01:12:01,818
Yeah, I totally get it.

1436
01:12:01,901 --> 01:12:03,528
Do you?

1437
01:12:03,611 --> 01:12:06,740
That really hit me hard yesterday.

1438
01:12:08,241 --> 01:12:10,994
So… yeah. Maybe it's time

1439
01:12:11,077 --> 01:12:13,038
I finally move on from chasing her.

1440
01:12:13,121 --> 01:12:14,456
We might as well be friends.

1441
01:12:14,539 --> 01:12:15,623
Yeah, Yoko-chan…

1442
01:12:15,915 --> 01:12:20,086
Seeing her with that starry-eyed,
in-love look again…

1443
01:12:20,170 --> 01:12:23,798
it feels pretty impossible.

1444
01:12:26,051 --> 01:12:29,345
I mean, it's not like this show is just
"Win Back Your Ex."

1445
01:12:29,429 --> 01:12:30,805
Right.

1446
01:12:30,889 --> 01:12:31,723
Yeah.

1447
01:12:31,806 --> 01:12:35,769
All I was doing was obsessing over how to

1448
01:12:35,852 --> 01:12:37,979
get back together with my ex.

1449
01:12:38,063 --> 01:12:39,898
I thought that's what

1450
01:12:39,981 --> 01:12:41,983
you were trying to do.

1451
01:12:42,817 --> 01:12:45,403
So when I realized
I wanted to see who else is out there,

1452
01:12:46,821 --> 01:12:48,490
I knew I wanted to ask you out.

1453
01:12:48,573 --> 01:12:50,075
Oh, really?

1454
01:12:50,867 --> 01:12:52,619
I think that's a good call.

1455
01:12:53,745 --> 01:12:55,413
I just wanted to tell you that.

1456
01:12:55,497 --> 01:12:59,667
I was hoping we could go,
and the timing just lined up.

1457
01:13:00,126 --> 01:13:01,669
And being around Yoko

1458
01:13:01,753 --> 01:13:03,546
was getting draining for me.

1459
01:13:03,880 --> 01:13:05,882
So thanks for coming over.

1460
01:13:06,758 --> 01:13:10,512
You've always got that
"I'm exhausted" look in your eyes.

1461
01:13:12,013 --> 01:13:13,515
Just a timid guy…

1462
01:13:14,557 --> 01:13:15,934
That's me.

1463
01:13:21,856 --> 01:13:26,486
We've both spent way too much time
obsessing over our exes…

1464
01:13:26,569 --> 01:13:28,404
Instead of that…

1465
01:13:29,280 --> 01:13:30,698
Want to face me?

1466
01:13:30,824 --> 01:13:33,368
Let's have a conversation.

1467
01:13:33,576 --> 01:13:35,453
Go on a date!

1468
01:13:37,622 --> 01:13:39,666
They're still in there?

1469
01:13:39,749 --> 01:13:41,084
Yeah, they are.

1470
01:13:41,167 --> 01:13:44,170
Are they really hitting it off that much?

1471
01:13:45,088 --> 01:13:48,758
What do they even have to talk about?

1472
01:13:54,180 --> 01:13:55,807
You said you can't swim.

1473
01:13:55,890 --> 01:13:56,891
I can swim!

1474
01:14:00,645 --> 01:14:01,604
They look nice.

1475
01:14:01,688 --> 01:14:03,314
Lovely pair.

1476
01:14:05,191 --> 01:14:06,317
No way.

1477
01:14:13,825 --> 01:14:16,953
This might be the most fun
I've had this whole trip.

1478
01:14:18,413 --> 01:14:20,415
Good to hear.

1479
01:14:20,498 --> 01:14:22,458
If only this happened earlier on…

1480
01:14:22,542 --> 01:14:24,377
His feelings were unrequited for so long.

1481
01:14:24,669 --> 01:14:27,797
The contrast with my ex is
so night and day.

1482
01:14:28,339 --> 01:14:30,341
How could I not fall for it?

1483
01:14:30,717 --> 01:14:34,179
I realized I'd never laughed so hard

1484
01:14:34,387 --> 01:14:37,056
that I cried. That never happened.

1485
01:14:37,182 --> 01:14:38,016
With your ex?

1486
01:14:38,099 --> 01:14:39,225
Maybe I never had fun.

1487
01:14:40,435 --> 01:14:43,521
Everyone says he's funny,

1488
01:14:43,605 --> 01:14:45,773
but I don't get it at all.

1489
01:14:46,149 --> 01:14:48,735
It's that airheaded vibe of his
you can't stand, right?

1490
01:14:48,902 --> 01:14:49,903
Is he an airhead?

1491
01:14:49,986 --> 01:14:51,029
He's an absolute total airhead.

1492
01:14:51,112 --> 01:14:52,989
Really? Is that so?

1493
01:14:53,072 --> 01:14:54,324
Professor Airhead.

1494
01:14:54,407 --> 01:14:55,742
Professor Airhead, huh.

1495
01:14:57,118 --> 01:14:58,828
I just don't get it.

1496
01:14:59,913 --> 01:15:01,456
Me too.

1497
01:15:01,581 --> 01:15:03,458
Haven't seen him smile like that in ages.

1498
01:15:03,541 --> 01:15:04,751
True.

1499
01:15:04,834 --> 01:15:07,086
Look at him cracking up!

1500
01:15:07,462 --> 01:15:08,963
Good for him.

1501
01:15:09,047 --> 01:15:10,131
He's asleep.

1502
01:15:10,882 --> 01:15:12,717
Oji.

1503
01:15:17,555 --> 01:15:18,723
Shit.

1504
01:15:19,474 --> 01:15:20,850
I passed out.

1505
01:15:24,938 --> 01:15:29,651
Things really blew wide open
right at the tail end of this vacation.

1506
01:15:29,734 --> 01:15:30,902
It's Okinawa magic.

1507
01:15:30,985 --> 01:15:31,903
Right.

1508
01:15:32,278 --> 01:15:35,240
That hot tub scene was great.

1509
01:15:35,323 --> 01:15:38,493
It's like Hiroyoshi finally broke free

1510
01:15:38,576 --> 01:15:40,411
from Yoko's spell.

1511
01:15:40,495 --> 01:15:42,956
Seeing him laughing with
his whole mouth open…

1512
01:15:43,539 --> 01:15:44,540
made me so happy.

1513
01:15:44,624 --> 01:15:47,335
Getting that sudden shot of pure,
fun romance energy.

1514
01:15:47,794 --> 01:15:51,297
Like Hiroyoshi-san said,

1515
01:15:51,381 --> 01:15:54,050
this isn't just a 'win back your ex' game.

1516
01:15:54,133 --> 01:15:56,177
I caught myself looking at it

1517
01:15:56,261 --> 01:15:57,470
that way too, wondering

1518
01:15:57,553 --> 01:15:59,055
if they would get back together.

1519
01:15:59,138 --> 01:16:00,848
The ex-bond is super strong.

1520
01:16:00,932 --> 01:16:05,270
Right, but that's not all this is.
They're free to go on a date.

1521
01:16:05,353 --> 01:16:07,355
Ryo and Mao went on a date too.

1522
01:16:07,438 --> 01:16:08,773
Yeah.

1523
01:16:08,856 --> 01:16:10,900
Mao looked like
she was having a total blast.

1524
01:16:11,150 --> 01:16:14,487
Maybe the door isn't completely

1525
01:16:14,570 --> 01:16:16,739
closed with Hikaru,

1526
01:16:16,823 --> 01:16:19,450
but even if she goes back to him,

1527
01:16:20,368 --> 01:16:23,579
she can at least see what else is

1528
01:16:23,663 --> 01:16:25,248
out there first.

1529
01:16:25,915 --> 01:16:27,542
This is where everything starts.

1530
01:16:27,625 --> 01:16:29,252
How many days do they have left?

1531
01:16:30,878 --> 01:16:32,505
Wow, this place is chic!

1532
01:16:32,755 --> 01:16:35,216
Talk about an ocean view.

1533
01:16:35,300 --> 01:16:38,052
'Ocean view' doesn't even do it justice.

1534
01:16:38,136 --> 01:16:39,887
It's unreal.

1535
01:16:40,388 --> 01:16:42,056
So gorgeous.

1536
01:16:42,932 --> 01:16:44,100
Alright.

1537
01:16:44,183 --> 01:16:45,018
Thanks.

1538
01:16:45,143 --> 01:16:47,061
Our first beer today. Cheers.

1539
01:16:47,437 --> 01:16:48,563
That's too low.

1540
01:16:49,188 --> 01:16:50,440
First sip.

1541
01:16:50,523 --> 01:16:51,899
So good.

1542
01:16:52,817 --> 01:16:53,901
Delicious.

1543
01:16:53,985 --> 01:16:55,236
Tastes so good.

1544
01:16:56,404 --> 01:16:58,698
Let's dig in.

1545
01:16:59,032 --> 01:17:00,283
Wanna try the pork?

1546
01:17:00,366 --> 01:17:01,367
The piggy?

1547
01:17:01,451 --> 01:17:02,869
Alright, piggy it is.

1548
01:17:05,997 --> 01:17:07,415
I'm kinda nervous.

1549
01:17:07,498 --> 01:17:08,333
Is it good?

1550
01:17:08,416 --> 01:17:09,250
So good.

1551
01:17:10,293 --> 01:17:12,503
You said you wanted to fall in love.

1552
01:17:13,713 --> 01:17:16,174
Is that actually happening for you here?

1553
01:17:17,675 --> 01:17:19,677
It's tough.

1554
01:17:20,261 --> 01:17:22,305
What are you planning to do on this trip?

1555
01:17:23,556 --> 01:17:24,891
I don't know.

1556
01:17:24,974 --> 01:17:26,351
I just get so burnt out.

1557
01:17:28,311 --> 01:17:30,021
Too many things to think about.

1558
01:17:30,313 --> 01:17:33,107
That's definitely a bad habit of mine.

1559
01:17:34,859 --> 01:17:37,904
What should I do… But…

1560
01:17:38,112 --> 01:17:42,325
the more you overthink, the more

1561
01:17:42,408 --> 01:17:44,285
you lose the plot anyway.

1562
01:17:45,661 --> 01:17:48,706
So today, I just wanted to have fun.

1563
01:17:48,790 --> 01:17:51,292
And when I thought about

1564
01:17:51,376 --> 01:17:52,835
who I'd enjoy being around,

1565
01:17:52,919 --> 01:17:54,629
you were hands-down my top pick.

1566
01:17:54,879 --> 01:17:55,880
Thank you!

1567
01:17:55,963 --> 01:17:57,465
For real. I mean it.

1568
01:17:59,384 --> 01:18:02,762
I wanted to see that youthful,
girlie side of you.

1569
01:18:03,721 --> 01:18:06,891
The fish date was awesome.

1570
01:18:07,141 --> 01:18:07,975
Was I acting like a girl?

1571
01:18:08,059 --> 01:18:08,935
Yeah.

1572
01:18:09,018 --> 01:18:10,353
You were all bubbly and giddy.

1573
01:18:10,436 --> 01:18:11,896
That's the real me deep down,

1574
01:18:14,190 --> 01:18:15,316
probably.

1575
01:18:15,566 --> 01:18:19,404
Honestly, I feel like it's way easier

1576
01:18:20,071 --> 01:18:23,157
talking to you in a chill,
casual spot like this.

1577
01:18:23,241 --> 01:18:26,994
I kinda dig this side of you.

1578
01:18:28,079 --> 01:18:30,957
He got to see a whole new side of her.

1579
01:18:31,582 --> 01:18:33,251
It was fun.

1580
01:18:38,339 --> 01:18:41,801
I think she actually just wants to
fall head over heels.

1581
01:18:41,884 --> 01:18:47,682
But with everything
she's carrying right now, it's tough.

1582
01:18:47,890 --> 01:18:51,185
It's not like I can just fix it
all on my own.

1583
01:18:52,270 --> 01:18:55,606
So I realized I really can't

1584
01:18:56,065 --> 01:18:57,358
rush her.

1585
01:18:57,567 --> 01:19:01,195
Even if I catch serious feelings for her,

1586
01:19:01,279 --> 01:19:05,324
I'm not gonna be like,
"Hey, let's make this official."

1587
01:19:05,616 --> 01:19:07,910
I just really wanna be there for her.

1588
01:19:07,994 --> 01:19:11,164
Guess this is a totally different dynamic
than before.

1589
01:19:11,581 --> 01:19:16,669
Don't push yourself too hard, okay?

1590
01:19:16,836 --> 01:19:18,754
Don't overthink it.

1591
01:19:19,172 --> 01:19:22,800
Obviously there are things

1592
01:19:23,009 --> 01:19:25,678
that you can't compromise, but…

1593
01:19:26,804 --> 01:19:29,056
Just let yourself be that
carefree, giddy Mao.

1594
01:19:30,391 --> 01:19:33,102
If you want to hit up gachapon machines,

1595
01:19:33,186 --> 01:19:35,021
I'll take you as many times as you want.

1596
01:19:36,063 --> 01:19:38,733
Hearing you say that
really helps right now.

1597
01:19:40,276 --> 01:19:41,819
It hit me today…

1598
01:19:41,903 --> 01:19:44,947
you don't need to rush things.

1599
01:19:47,617 --> 01:19:50,453
Just work through stuff one by one.

1600
01:19:51,412 --> 01:19:53,206
And…

1601
01:19:55,458 --> 01:19:57,210
Well…

1602
01:19:57,293 --> 01:20:00,171
Whenever I'm with you,
I'll make sure we're having fun.

1603
01:20:00,755 --> 01:20:04,634
You might never see this

1604
01:20:04,800 --> 01:20:07,470
super mellow version of me again.

1605
01:20:07,762 --> 01:20:09,931
Super chill Ryo-chan is rare.

1606
01:20:10,139 --> 01:20:12,099
Like right now…

1607
01:20:12,266 --> 01:20:13,434
"Mao."

1608
01:20:13,643 --> 01:20:16,145
Say this is Level 1.

1609
01:20:16,437 --> 01:20:17,480
"Mao-chan!"

1610
01:20:17,563 --> 01:20:19,982
This energy is Level 10. Just tell me

1611
01:20:20,066 --> 01:20:22,235
what level you want today,

1612
01:20:22,318 --> 01:20:24,153
and I'll match it.

1613
01:20:24,237 --> 01:20:25,530
You'll do that for me?

1614
01:20:25,905 --> 01:20:26,864
You'll match my energy?

1615
01:20:26,948 --> 01:20:27,782
I will.

1616
01:20:27,907 --> 01:20:29,492
I want Level 10 Ryo-chan right now.

1617
01:20:29,575 --> 01:20:31,410
You got it!

1618
01:20:33,037 --> 01:20:34,372
So sweet.

1619
01:20:36,207 --> 01:20:39,001
But seriously, there is zero reason
for you to stay in a funk.

1620
01:20:39,585 --> 01:20:40,878
Let's stay positive.

1621
01:20:41,170 --> 01:20:42,505
Positive looks good on you.

1622
01:20:44,465 --> 01:20:45,550
I will.

1623
01:20:45,675 --> 01:20:47,385
Positive Mao is the best.

1624
01:20:49,095 --> 01:20:51,222
He's so kind.

1625
01:20:54,141 --> 01:20:57,186
Yesterday I talked through
a bunch of stuff with Mao,

1626
01:20:57,562 --> 01:21:00,731
and we had a really great time.

1627
01:21:01,232 --> 01:21:03,651
And after that, last night…

1628
01:21:04,068 --> 01:21:06,696
we had that email mission, right?

1629
01:21:06,779 --> 01:21:08,573
And I…

1630
01:21:08,656 --> 01:21:10,074
I sent mine to Mao.

1631
01:21:10,908 --> 01:21:13,119
But I didn't get one from her.

1632
01:21:13,536 --> 01:21:14,787
I see.

1633
01:21:14,870 --> 01:21:16,706
Maybe she didn't send it to anyone.

1634
01:21:16,789 --> 01:21:20,710
Who knows. Maybe there's someone else
catching her eye.

1635
01:21:20,793 --> 01:21:22,295
And so…

1636
01:21:22,461 --> 01:21:26,007
After I laid everything on the line,
getting that kind of response…

1637
01:21:26,090 --> 01:21:28,593
Zero clue what she's thinking.
Haven't seen her today.

1638
01:21:28,676 --> 01:21:31,178
She just slipped out
without saying a word.

1639
01:21:31,262 --> 01:21:32,888
She went on a date.

1640
01:21:32,972 --> 01:21:34,348
So she might've asked someone out.

1641
01:21:34,473 --> 01:21:36,559
Last time she went out with Ryo,

1642
01:21:36,642 --> 01:21:38,561
she just vanished and that was that.

1643
01:21:39,353 --> 01:21:42,189
So if that's how she plays it,

1644
01:21:42,690 --> 01:21:46,110
I don't see why I should bother
putting my feelings out there.

1645
01:21:46,402 --> 01:21:47,361
Why give up?

1646
01:21:49,405 --> 01:21:50,906
Right?

1647
01:21:53,034 --> 01:21:55,536
So you're starting to waver on her.

1648
01:21:55,620 --> 01:21:59,248
We talked about her dealbreakers,

1649
01:22:00,249 --> 01:22:01,542
and yesterday's email…

1650
01:22:01,626 --> 01:22:03,586
I mean, it said "spark", so…

1651
01:22:04,253 --> 01:22:07,214
maybe she just doesn't
feel that spark with me.

1652
01:22:07,840 --> 01:22:10,635
It's hard to feel that spark with
someone you were married to.

1653
01:22:10,718 --> 01:22:11,927
But for me,

1654
01:22:12,011 --> 01:22:14,263
if there's no spark in a marriage,

1655
01:22:14,347 --> 01:22:15,931
what's even the point?

1656
01:22:16,015 --> 01:22:17,516
That's how I feel.

1657
01:22:17,600 --> 01:22:19,435
You need spark, not just comfort.

1658
01:22:19,935 --> 01:22:24,106
Honestly, it's not as simple as
"do I like her or not,"

1659
01:22:24,315 --> 01:22:27,735
but that spark is what makes you
want to fight for it.

1660
01:22:29,362 --> 01:22:31,781
Turns out your personality is
more intense than mine.

1661
01:22:31,864 --> 01:22:34,241
I'm intense.

1662
01:22:38,204 --> 01:22:40,790
As long as everyone else is happy.

1663
01:22:42,958 --> 01:22:44,460
Really?

1664
01:22:47,588 --> 01:22:48,506
No, no.

1665
01:22:48,589 --> 01:22:51,467
It's not about "spark".

1666
01:22:55,096 --> 01:22:56,097
They're back.

1667
01:22:56,180 --> 01:22:57,014
Hey.

1668
01:22:57,098 --> 01:22:58,391
Hey.

1669
01:22:58,474 --> 01:22:59,308
We're back.

1670
01:22:59,684 --> 01:23:00,851
How'd it go?

1671
01:23:00,935 --> 01:23:02,520
His energy was through the roof.

1672
01:23:03,854 --> 01:23:05,022
It was the highest yet.

1673
01:23:05,106 --> 01:23:07,108
Their styles are actually in sync.

1674
01:23:07,525 --> 01:23:08,943
This must be hard for Misato.

1675
01:23:09,026 --> 01:23:10,653
Misato…

1676
01:23:11,153 --> 01:23:12,863
First time anyone's ever said that to us.

1677
01:23:12,947 --> 01:23:14,365
Yeah.

1678
01:23:14,448 --> 01:23:16,534
Alright, get me a drink too.

1679
01:23:16,617 --> 01:23:18,119
Sure thing.

1680
01:23:18,202 --> 01:23:20,955
Just sit down. I'll get it for you.

1681
01:23:23,708 --> 01:23:25,835
Welcome back!

1682
01:23:26,085 --> 01:23:28,921
Welcome back.

1683
01:23:29,755 --> 01:23:30,881
I just got back too.

1684
01:23:30,965 --> 01:23:32,007
Did you get a bit tan?

1685
01:23:32,174 --> 01:23:33,634
Did you get tanned?

1686
01:23:34,135 --> 01:23:35,094
Or is it the booze?

1687
01:23:35,177 --> 01:23:36,303
Your ears are red.

1688
01:23:36,721 --> 01:23:37,888
What do you want to drink?

1689
01:23:42,184 --> 01:23:44,437
Can't we hit the jacuzzi
over there tomorrow?

1690
01:23:44,520 --> 01:23:45,438
We used it today.

1691
01:23:45,521 --> 01:23:46,355
You did?

1692
01:23:46,439 --> 01:23:47,440
With Hiroyoshi.

1693
01:23:47,523 --> 01:23:49,191
Did you see her in a swimsuit?

1694
01:23:49,275 --> 01:23:50,401
Yeah, totally.

1695
01:23:50,484 --> 01:23:51,318
Swimsuit?

1696
01:23:51,777 --> 01:23:54,029
Sneaking off, huh?

1697
01:23:54,989 --> 01:23:56,323
We snuck off.

1698
01:23:56,407 --> 01:23:58,492
Didn't I say I was gonna sneak off first?

1699
01:23:59,660 --> 01:24:01,454
Sorry, sorry. Really.

1700
01:24:01,871 --> 01:24:03,581
My bad.

1701
01:24:05,833 --> 01:24:09,503
Hikaru took a pretty heavy hit there.

1702
01:24:14,008 --> 01:24:16,761
Guess this old guy
shouldn't get ahead of himself.

1703
01:24:16,844 --> 01:24:18,345
Nobody said that.

1704
01:24:18,429 --> 01:24:21,015
I definitely didn't say that.

1705
01:24:22,475 --> 01:24:23,893
Oh, this.

1706
01:24:32,485 --> 01:24:34,028
I'm exhausted, heading to bed.

1707
01:24:34,111 --> 01:24:35,905
Night.

1708
01:24:36,155 --> 01:24:37,490
He's going?

1709
01:24:48,417 --> 01:24:51,045
He's totally sulking,
which is such a hassle.

1710
01:24:51,378 --> 01:24:54,048
I could go over to his room right now

1711
01:24:54,548 --> 01:24:58,302
and ask what his deal is,

1712
01:24:58,552 --> 01:25:01,388
but if I do, I'm just bailing him out.

1713
01:25:01,472 --> 01:25:03,641
So I'm drawing the line tonight.

1714
01:25:04,141 --> 01:25:05,309
Good call.

1715
01:25:05,392 --> 01:25:07,186
She's got his entire playbook

1716
01:25:07,269 --> 01:25:08,854
completely figured out.

1717
01:25:12,399 --> 01:25:13,484
How are things with Hikaru?

1718
01:25:16,487 --> 01:25:17,822
For us,

1719
01:25:17,905 --> 01:25:21,909
Okinawa is where all our memories are.

1720
01:25:21,992 --> 01:25:25,663
It really just felt like reminiscing about

1721
01:25:25,746 --> 01:25:28,707
our dates back before we had kids.

1722
01:25:28,791 --> 01:25:30,042
At the end

1723
01:25:30,125 --> 01:25:33,295
he was like, "It made me realize
I want to be by your side

1724
01:25:33,379 --> 01:25:34,630
forever."

1725
01:25:34,713 --> 01:25:38,175
He's always been the type who feels like
opening up hits his pride,

1726
01:25:38,884 --> 01:25:42,513
so the fact that
he said all that on his own

1727
01:25:42,596 --> 01:25:44,765
meant a lot to me.

1728
01:25:44,849 --> 01:25:45,683
Yeah.

1729
01:25:45,766 --> 01:25:46,976
Did that move you?

1730
01:25:47,685 --> 01:25:50,271
The fact that he actually
put his feelings into words…

1731
01:25:50,396 --> 01:25:52,982
It definitely reached me.

1732
01:25:55,025 --> 01:25:56,360
As of yesterday,

1733
01:25:56,443 --> 01:25:59,363
part of me was thinking
maybe we could get back together.

1734
01:26:00,406 --> 01:26:01,574
But…

1735
01:26:01,657 --> 01:26:05,286
to actually make that leap…

1736
01:26:05,369 --> 01:26:07,454
where we're at right now is
nowhere near enough.

1737
01:26:07,538 --> 01:26:09,748
Just history repeating itself
all over again.

1738
01:26:09,999 --> 01:26:14,837
So even if we got back together,
it wouldn't be right away.

1739
01:26:14,920 --> 01:26:18,757
It'd be like a trial run for a year or two

1740
01:26:19,049 --> 01:26:22,219
to see if he can actually stick

1741
01:26:22,303 --> 01:26:24,138
to my terms.

1742
01:26:24,221 --> 01:26:26,098
Are those realistic conditions for him?

1743
01:26:26,473 --> 01:26:29,476
To normal couples

1744
01:26:29,560 --> 01:26:31,645
it might seem like basic stuff,

1745
01:26:31,729 --> 01:26:34,315
but for us,

1746
01:26:34,648 --> 01:26:36,108
it wasn't normal.

1747
01:26:36,191 --> 01:26:39,653
Living apart was the norm,

1748
01:26:41,447 --> 01:26:46,160
so I need to really pin down
those details.

1749
01:26:46,702 --> 01:26:48,454
Honestly,

1750
01:26:48,537 --> 01:26:50,873
that's a good thing for Hikaru too.

1751
01:26:51,373 --> 01:26:53,918
Setting clear boundaries and stepping up

1752
01:26:54,001 --> 01:26:57,922
will actually make him a better person.

1753
01:26:58,505 --> 01:27:03,177
He should fight for it, for his own sake.

1754
01:27:03,302 --> 01:27:04,345
But…

1755
01:27:04,428 --> 01:27:07,264
even if I move on to someone new,

1756
01:27:07,348 --> 01:27:09,642
he's still the kids' dad.

1757
01:27:10,309 --> 01:27:13,854
Co-parenting,

1758
01:27:13,938 --> 01:27:16,440
the responsibility, the financial side…

1759
01:27:16,607 --> 01:27:20,778
I'm still gonna expect him to
hold up his end.

1760
01:27:20,861 --> 01:27:24,156
Even if I move on and get a new boyfriend,

1761
01:27:24,239 --> 01:27:26,408
he needs to wrap his head around

1762
01:27:26,492 --> 01:27:29,578
how we keep our dynamic working.

1763
01:27:29,828 --> 01:27:33,415
I tried to lay it on the line.

1764
01:27:33,499 --> 01:27:35,084
I wonder if it sank in.

1765
01:27:35,751 --> 01:27:38,420
I hope so.

1766
01:27:41,924 --> 01:27:44,218
I know I have to deal with it,

1767
01:27:44,301 --> 01:27:47,179
but part of me just wants to run away.

1768
01:27:48,722 --> 01:27:51,642
It's so exhausting.

1769
01:27:54,144 --> 01:27:57,690
It was getting really heavy.

1770
01:27:59,525 --> 01:28:02,403
So having someone comfort me
meant everything.

1771
01:28:04,571 --> 01:28:08,909
Talk about perfect timing today.

1772
01:28:08,993 --> 01:28:11,412
Ryo really came to the rescue.

1773
01:28:12,788 --> 01:28:16,417
Just keeping things light

1774
01:28:18,002 --> 01:28:19,962
with casual banter…

1775
01:28:21,005 --> 01:28:26,552
that's been such a lifeline for me.

1776
01:28:27,928 --> 01:28:29,471
Yeah.

1777
01:28:30,472 --> 01:28:33,517
Right now, I have to face
harsh reality with Hikaru.

1778
01:28:33,600 --> 01:28:35,853
The money, the kids…

1779
01:28:35,936 --> 01:28:39,648
Those are real issues I can't ignore,

1780
01:28:39,773 --> 01:28:42,860
but I've been backing myself
into a corner.

1781
01:28:43,736 --> 01:28:47,781
And in the middle of all that pressure,
I felt zero peace.

1782
01:28:49,116 --> 01:28:52,327
If I could just start fresh

1783
01:28:52,411 --> 01:28:56,790
with someone with zero baggage,

1784
01:28:56,874 --> 01:29:00,294
I wouldn't have half as much
on my mind right now.

1785
01:29:00,377 --> 01:29:04,631
Going for a guy who gives me

1786
01:29:04,715 --> 01:29:07,468
a breather from reality

1787
01:29:07,551 --> 01:29:10,679
might actually be a good move.

1788
01:29:11,013 --> 01:29:13,640
I kind of just thought…

1789
01:29:13,766 --> 01:29:17,770
starting something new

1790
01:29:17,978 --> 01:29:21,231
with zero pressure might be

1791
01:29:21,315 --> 01:29:24,693
a nice way to clear my head.

1792
01:29:25,194 --> 01:29:26,904
Right.

1793
01:29:27,696 --> 01:29:30,449
That's how I feel.

1794
01:29:31,116 --> 01:29:32,743
I'd like about another year.

1795
01:29:33,035 --> 01:29:34,828
Yeah, totally understand.

1796
01:29:34,912 --> 01:29:36,705
It really takes time.

1797
01:29:36,789 --> 01:29:38,373
Right.

1798
01:29:38,457 --> 01:29:42,169
And Ryo was saying
he shouldn't rush things,

1799
01:29:42,252 --> 01:29:45,464
so their timing lines up perfectly.

1800
01:29:51,637 --> 01:29:52,971
So hot.

1801
01:29:54,973 --> 01:29:57,226
Hikaru. Morning.

1802
01:30:02,773 --> 01:30:04,024
Silent treatment?

1803
01:30:04,775 --> 01:30:06,360
Why are you mad? What happened?

1804
01:30:06,443 --> 01:30:07,319
I'm not mad at all.

1805
01:30:07,402 --> 01:30:08,445
Today's the final day!

1806
01:30:08,529 --> 01:30:09,905
No time to be sleeping in.

1807
01:30:09,988 --> 01:30:12,157
Didn't you say you were ready to
roll with the punches?

1808
01:30:12,908 --> 01:30:16,286
For me, the spark and the butterflies
have to come first.

1809
01:30:16,370 --> 01:30:18,705
Real-world issues and butterflies
are two different things.

1810
01:30:18,789 --> 01:30:21,542
If that's how it is,
I'm just heading overseas.

1811
01:30:21,625 --> 01:30:23,544
So that's where your mind's at.

1812
01:30:26,713 --> 01:30:28,799
I want to feel those butterflies again.

1813
01:30:29,466 --> 01:30:32,886
When exes try to make it work,

1814
01:30:32,970 --> 01:30:34,429
isn't that the only thing
that truly matters?

1815
01:30:35,139 --> 01:30:38,725
Going back to being friends
isn't an option.

1816
01:30:39,852 --> 01:30:41,687
I can't trust him.

1817
01:30:51,029 --> 01:30:53,574
This is the exact kind of romance
I've been looking for.

1818
01:30:54,616 --> 01:30:56,827
Even with my ex around,

1819
01:30:57,369 --> 01:30:58,787
I'm completely unbothered.

1820
01:31:02,749 --> 01:31:04,543
I want you to be my girlfriend.

1821
01:31:08,297 --> 01:31:09,756
I realized I love her.

1822
01:31:09,840 --> 01:31:11,425
I'm completely all-in on her now.

1823
01:31:11,675 --> 01:31:15,220
She was so precious to me.
Words couldn't even describe it.

1824
01:31:15,470 --> 01:31:19,224
She'd probably be happier
with someone else.

1825
01:31:19,766 --> 01:31:23,896
Whatever comes our way,
I know we can overcome it together.

1826
01:31:46,752 --> 01:31:49,296
Amazing! It actually paid off!
